/* Authored Forgewick conversations. Each row has three complete, independent
   Corin/response pairs. No legacy topic or generated reply pool is reused. */
const FORGEWICK_DIALOGUE_CAST=(()=>{
  const cast={};
  const t=(title,first,...replies)=>({title,first,replies});
  const p=(name,role,bio,meeting,hello,news,back,...rows)=>cast[name]={role,bio,meeting,hello,news,back,rows};

p('Prue','Stonemason','A young mason who enjoys ambitious designs and distrusts anyone who mistakes her age for inexperience.',
 ['Oh! I was about to ask you to move along, and then your dragon looked at me. I’m Prue. Let me start that welcome again.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius. We were hoping to have a look around without frightening everyone.', 'You have caught me by surprise, that is all. Welcome to Forgewick, both of you.'],
 'I’m Prue. If you are looking for a mason, you have found one. If you are looking for directions, I am cheaper than a mason.',
 'Travelling with a dragon? That explains why an ordinary road might feel rather narrow. I would like to meet him sometime.',
 'Hello again. I have time for a proper conversation, if you do.',
 t('Do you choose the shapes of the buildings?', 'I would like to build a covered meeting place with broad steps. Most commissions begin with the cost of stone; I want to begin with how people would use it.',
 ['Who would the meeting place be for?', 'Anyone who wanted company or shelter. Somewhere people could gather without paying for a drink.'],
 ['Would that make it more expensive?', 'Not necessarily. A well-placed opening can do more for a room than expensive decoration.'],
 ['I never thought about how a building feels.', 'Think of the first house you were glad to reach in the rain. You understood it before anybody explained it.']),
 t('Do people underestimate you?', 'A customer once asked when the mason would arrive while I was explaining his estimate. I made him ask the question twice.',
 ['What did you say the second time?', 'That the mason was waiting for him to finish. We got along better after that.'],
 ['Did you still take the job?', 'Yes. His money was perfectly capable of recognising me.'],
 ['I get called “boy” more often than Corin.', 'Then I shall use Corin. It is no great hardship to learn a name.']),
 t('Would a dragon damage the streets?', 'People will blame the first cracked paving stone on Aurelius. I know which ones were cracked before you arrived.',
 ['Will you tell them that?', 'Certainly. I laid some of the replacements. I am not losing credit for the work or blaming him for the delay.'],
 ['We are trying to keep out of everyone’s way.', 'A little care is enough. You are allowed to use the street too.'],
 ['Could you make paving strong enough for dragons?', 'Given time and a proper foundation. I would enjoy a commission that ambitious.']),
 t('What work does the crown ask for?', 'Royal jobs arrive with a deadline and the expectation that every other repair can wait. A leaking roof does not care whose seal is on the order.',
 ['Can you refuse an order?', 'Not without making trouble for the whole workshop. That is why I want the system changed, not merely a kinder foreman.'],
 ['What gets postponed?', 'Small repairs. The ones a wealthy visitor never notices and the people living with them notice every day.'],
 ['That sounds exhausting.', 'It is. I still like being a mason. I would like to spend more of the day doing it.']),
 t('I wanted to hear more about your meeting place.', 'You remembered! I have settled on an open-sided roof. People should be able to see their friends arriving.',
 ['Leave a wide way in for us.', 'For Aurelius? Gladly. That is a useful improvement to the plan, not a ceremonial dragon entrance.'],
 ['Who would pay for it?', 'Several small subscriptions, if I can persuade the town. I do not want one rich donor deciding who may sit there.'],
 ['Would you put your name on it?', 'On a small stone somewhere. I am allowed to be pleased with my work.']));

p('Toft','Miner and provisions merchant','An ex-miner who stocks useful supplies and enjoys haggling almost as much as talking about food.',
 ['I was going to offer you provisions, but I may need to think in larger portions. That is a dragon, isn’t it? Toft, at your service.', 'I’m Corin, and he is Aurelius. Normal portions will do for me. We can talk supplies after saying hello.'],
 'Toft. Supplies are my business, but looking costs nothing. What brings you through Forgewick?',
 'A dragon on the journey as well? Then it is sensible to keep both your meals in mind. I can help with provisions when you want them.',
 'Good to see you, Corin. Shopping, or giving an old miner an excuse to talk?',
 t('What should I buy before travelling?', 'Buy for the trouble you actually expect. A potion you remember to use is worth more than an expensive item you do not understand.',
 ['What would you put first?', 'Healing for yourself and food for Aurelius. Then look at the other supplies and decide what suits you.'],
 ['Should I spend all my gold now?', 'Leave yourself some coin for the next town. I enjoy a sale, but I prefer customers who make it that far.'],
 ['Will you mind if I only look?', 'I will survive the disappointment. Ask to purchase whenever you want to see my stock.']),
 t('Do you miss being a miner?', 'The work, sometimes. The meal afterwards, often. Nothing improves a disappointing stew like having climbed out of a mine to reach it.',
 ['Was the stew always disappointing?', 'Only when I cooked. I had a short and unsuccessful reign as camp cook.'],
 ['What part of the work do you miss?', 'Knowing the next person understood exactly what my day had been like. We needed fewer words at supper.'],
 ['Do the miners still visit you?', 'Yes. They inspect my prices with the same suspicion we once reserved for a questionable tunnel.']),
 t('Do you charge more because of Aurelius?', 'No. The price is for the provisions, not for how astonishing the customer’s travelling companion happens to be.',
 ['I am glad I asked.', 'So am I. Better to settle it plainly than spend the whole visit wondering.'],
 ['You could have called it a dragon surcharge.', 'And then explained why I wanted a dragon to think me dishonest? An unwise business plan.'],
 ['He would appreciate being treated normally.', 'Then normally it is. Though I reserve the right to be impressed in private.']),
 t('Does the crown buy supplies here?', 'The crown is very fond of the word “requisition”. It makes taking someone’s stock sound like a discussion about paperwork.',
 ['Do you receive payment?', 'Not reliably. Meanwhile the people who supplied me still deserve theirs.'],
 ['How do you keep going?', 'I buy carefully, and neighbours settle what they owe when they can. I would rather keep that trust than squeeze it dry.'],
 ['Could I help by buying something?', 'Only if you need it. I am complaining about the crown, not inventing an obligation for you.']),
 t('Have you thought about another trade?', 'I have a very serious plan to judge pies. Apparently nobody wants to pay me simply to eat them.',
 ['Would you be a fair judge?', 'Absolutely. I would try each pie twice in case the first slice was misleading.'],
 ['Perhaps sell a few alongside your supplies.', 'Then I would have to stop myself eating the stock. You have found the flaw in the enterprise.'],
 ['I will remember you if we find a pie contest.', 'That is the sort of useful news I hoped a traveller would bring.']));

p('Ovid','Market organiser','Ovid keeps the market running, dislikes public fuss, and remembers the people hidden behind every delivery.',
 ['Hold a moment. Is the dragon with you? I’m Ovid; I help keep this market from becoming a collision.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius, and yes, we travel together. Tell me if we are blocking somebody’s way.', 'You are fine there. Thank you for asking before everybody began shouting advice.'],
 'Ovid. Are you looking for a particular trader, or finding your way around?',
 'A dragon as a travelling companion. That will give the market something to discuss besides prices. You are welcome to bring him through with care.',
 'Corin, hello. The market will manage without my supervision for a minute.',
 t('How do you settle a market argument?', 'I ask each person what they want to happen next. It is astonishing how often they have only prepared what they want to shout.',
 ['Does that work?', 'Often enough. Sometimes the answer is simply an apology, which would have saved us all twenty minutes.'],
 ['What if both people are right?', 'Then we look for a practical arrangement. Being right does not create another six feet of street.'],
 ['I am not good at keeping calm.', 'You can ask for a moment. You need not produce your finest sentence while someone is bellowing at you.']),
 t('What do you enjoy about the market?', 'The first delivery after somebody has been away. People pretend to inspect the goods while making sure the traveller is well.',
 ['Do they ever just say they missed them?', 'Eventually. Usually after complaining about how long the delivery took.'],
 ['Who notices if someone is missing?', 'More people than you might expect. Familiar routines can become a way of looking after one another.'],
 ['I hope Millwood does that when I return.', 'They will probably feed you before letting you finish your story. That is generally a good sign.']),
 t('What if people gather around Aurelius?', 'I can ask them to leave a passage. Curiosity is understandable; surrounding a visitor is still rude.',
 ['Thank you. He is not an attraction.', 'Agreed. If people want a conversation, they can begin by asking.'],
 ['I do not mind answering a few questions.', 'Then choose how many. You do not owe everyone in town an afternoon.'],
 ['What if somebody is frightened?', 'Give them room as well. Nobody learns much while being laughed at for their first reaction.']),
 t('Who decides the market rules?', 'Local traders can agree on almost everything until a royal officer arrives with a new exception for himself.',
 ['What kind of exception?', 'A cart in a passage everyone else must keep clear. A fee other people have to pay. Small privileges that make a crowded day harder.'],
 ['Do you challenge them?', 'I ask the question plainly, with witnesses. It does not always work, but pretending the rule was fair would work even less.'],
 ['What would you change first?', 'One set of rules, written clearly, with somebody ordinary allowed to question them.']),
 t('Do you ever take a day away?', 'I am planning one. My chief concern is that the market will run perfectly without me and I shall have to admit it.',
 ['That sounds like proof you did a good job.', 'It does, when you put it that way. I may borrow that explanation.'],
 ['Where would you go?', 'Somewhere I cannot see a delivery cart. A very modest ambition.'],
 ['Will you tell everyone beforehand?', 'Yes. Disappearing to prove a point would make a poor holiday and a worse example.']));

p('Garran','Metalworker','Garran makes small fittings, takes pride in useful work, and has a weakness for elaborate sporting competitions.',
 ['Those scales! Forgive me, I’m staring as if I could learn to forge them. Garran is my name.', 'I’m Corin. This is Aurelius. You may look, but please ask before trying to inspect him.', 'Fairly said. My curiosity got ahead of my manners.'],
 'Garran. I make fittings and repairs. What can I tell you?',
 'You travel with a dragon? I have spent too long imagining them from old metalwork. I should like to see the living creature someday.',
 'Hello, Corin. There is always time for a question that is not about a broken latch.',
 t('What is the smallest thing you make?', 'The little pins in a good hinge. People praise a grand door while the pins quietly do all the work.',
 ['Do you mind that?', 'Not much. If people notice a hinge every time they use it, the hinge probably needs fixing.'],
 ['Is small work harder?', 'Less room for an error. A fraction off at the bench becomes an irritating wobble for years.'],
 ['Have you made anything grand?', 'A pair of gates once. I still remember the pins more fondly than the gates.']),
 t('What do you do when work finishes?', 'Throw rings at a peg with people who insist it is a relaxing pastime. They become furious when I win.',
 ['Are you very good?', 'Adequate. My brother’s elaborate excuses do most of the entertaining.'],
 ['Do you make the rings too?', 'Yes, and everyone examines them whenever I have a lucky throw.'],
 ['I would probably miss the peg.', 'Most throws do. We enjoy several minutes of confidence before admitting that.']),
 t('Would you make armour for a dragon?', 'I would begin by asking what Aurelius actually needs. A smith can become so fond of metal that he starts solving problems nobody has.',
 ['His wings would need room.', 'Exactly. A fitting that restricts movement could be worse than the danger it was meant to prevent.'],
 ['Could you do it if he asked?', 'I would need to learn a great deal first. That is an honest answer, if a less impressive one.'],
 ['He has enough people deciding things for him.', 'Then I shall add no commission to his troubles.']),
 t('What happens when royal work takes priority?', 'A farmer once waited weeks for a replacement fitting while a royal order swallowed every hour we had.',
 ['Did you manage to help?', 'Eventually. By then the delay had cost him more than the fitting ever should.'],
 ['Why would the crown want that?', 'I doubt anyone considered him at all. That is often the trouble.'],
 ['Would you rather make tools than weapons?', 'I would rather choose. A tool in time can matter enormously to somebody.']),
 t('Have your neighbours asked you about us?', 'A few have. I told them you were willing to talk and that neither of you was obliged to perform a trick.',
 ['That is a better introduction than some.', 'I can imagine. Being interesting must become tiring when people mistake it for employment.'],
 ['Did anyone ask a sensible question?', 'A child asked whether dragons get bored. I thought that a better beginning than asking how hot their fire is.'],
 ['Aurelius would probably enjoy the ring game.', 'Then he can have a go if he wishes. My brother will immediately demand a rule about wings.']));

p('Nessa','Glass decorator','Nessa decorates finished glass in Forgewick, buys pieces from several makers, and enjoys colour for its own sake.',
 ['A real dragon. I have painted so many wrong ones on glass. I’m Nessa, and I owe your companion a better likeness.', 'Corin. His name is Aurelius. I expect he would like being asked what he thinks of a picture.', 'Of course. A subject with an opinion would be a welcome change.'],
 'Hello, I’m Nessa. I decorate glass, though I am perfectly happy to discuss other things.',
 'A dragon travels with you? Then some of the old pictures may finally meet a reliable critic. I hope I get the chance to ask him about them.',
 'Corin, hello. Have you brought a story, or shall I supply one?',
 t('How is decorated glass different from blowing it?', 'I work on pieces after they have been shaped. Choosing what belongs on a surface is a different skill from making the surface itself.',
 ['Whose glass do you work on?', 'Several makers’. I sometimes buy pieces from Sela, whose workshop is in Sandspire now, not here in Forgewick.'],
 ['Can you rescue an ugly piece?', 'Occasionally. Sometimes the kindest thing is to stop adding colours.'],
 ['What do you like painting?', 'Plants nobody bothers to name. People recognise them instantly and then argue about what to call them.']),
 t('Do customers choose strange designs?', 'One asked for a cup that looked full when it was empty. I told him the deception would last until he tried drinking.',
 ['Did he still want it?', 'Very much. Apparently confusing his brother was worth the expense.'],
 ['Could you make one?', 'I could paint the illusion from one angle. I warned him it was a joke, not sorcery.'],
 ['I would rather know when my cup was empty.', 'A sensible customer. Much less entertaining, but sensible.']),
 t('What would you put in Aurelius’s portrait?', 'Something he chooses. A favourite place, perhaps. I would rather learn what matters to him than surround him with invented flames.',
 ['He is curious about almost everything.', 'Then we may need a large surface.'],
 ['Could you paint the two of us together?', 'Yes. You could decide what you want remembered about the journey.'],
 ['People always make dragons look angry.', 'Anger is easy to suggest with sharp lines. A thoughtful face takes more attention.']),
 t('Does the dragon ban affect your work?', 'Customers ask for ordinary patterns now. I do not press them to explain why an old family design suddenly feels dangerous.',
 ['Have you stopped painting dragons?', 'I have stopped displaying those commissions. I resent having to make that distinction.'],
 ['Could somebody report a customer?', 'Yes. That is why their names are not stories for me to tell a visitor.'],
 ['What would you paint if the ban ended?', 'Whatever people asked for, without first discussing who might see it.']),
 t('What picture would you make for yourself?', 'A day at the coast. I have never been, and I would like to paint water I have actually seen.',
 ['Why not go?', 'Money, work, and the habit of postponing things. I am trying to separate the real obstacles from the familiar excuses.'],
 ['Would you take your paints?', 'Probably. I know myself too well to promise a holiday without them.'],
 ['I could tell you about Coralmere when I have been.', 'I would enjoy that. Especially the ordinary details a grand story forgets.']));

p('Kerr','Coal carrier','Kerr hauls fuel around Forgewick, keeps his humour on difficult days, and dreams of growing something delicate.',
 ['I thought the shadow was a cart coming up behind me. Then I looked up. Kerr. Give me a moment to stop being surprised.', 'I’m Corin, and that is Aurelius. We did not mean to startle you.', 'No harm done. I am glad I looked before giving a dragon directions to the coal yard.'],
 'Kerr. If you need directions, ask while I am stopped; I give much better answers when I can catch my breath.',
 'A dragon? I spend all day moving fuel, and you travel with someone who makes his own fire. There is a joke in that, but I will spare you until I find it.',
 'Hello again, Corin. A conversation sounds like a decent use of a rest.',
 t('How do you make a heavy load easier?', 'Plan where you will put it down before you lift it. Being determined is useful; having somewhere to stop is better.',
 ['Did somebody teach you that?', 'My aunt, after watching me get stranded with a sack in a very narrow passage.'],
 ['Does the work get easier?', 'You get better at judging it. The sack does not become lighter because you have had a birthday.'],
 ['I should think about our stops more.', 'Yes. Arriving exhausted is not a prize in itself.']),
 t('What would you grow in a garden?', 'Sweet peas. Delicate things that climb all over the place and refuse to look industrial.',
 ['Have you tried yet?', 'A small patch. The first year I congratulated myself on a fine crop of weeds.'],
 ['Why sweet peas?', 'My mother grew them. I would like something from her garden that survives my gardening.'],
 ['Would you sell the flowers?', 'No. I would like one thing I do not carry somewhere for money.']),
 t('Could Aurelius help with the work?', 'I would not ask him to haul coal just because he is strong. Everyone stronger than me deserves an afternoon off as well.',
 ['Thank you for thinking of it that way.', 'I have heard enough “you can manage one more load” for a lifetime.'],
 ['He might want to help somebody.', 'Then ask what help is useful before promising it. A willing helper still needs to know the job.'],
 ['Does it bother you when people call him useful?', 'Useful is a fine thing to be. It is a poor substitute for a name.']),
 t('Can workers afford a day off?', 'Sometimes we arrange a day between us. Royal quotas make that much harder; the work keeps its deadline when people run out of strength.',
 ['What happens to someone who cannot keep up?', 'Too often another worker carries the extra. We try to help, but that does not make the demand fair.'],
 ['Do you ever complain?', 'Yes. Quietly when I must, loudly when I can. Neither is a complete solution.'],
 ['What would improve things?', 'A wage that leaves room for being ill, and a foreman allowed to stop a dangerous job.']),
 t('How are the sweet peas going?', 'Better. I asked someone who actually gardens before doing anything dramatic this time.',
 ['Was the advice complicated?', 'Mostly “leave them alone for a day”. I found that surprisingly demanding.'],
 ['Have they flowered?', 'A few. I am trying not to show every passer-by the same three blossoms.'],
 ['You sound pleased.', 'I am. It is nice to finish a day with something growing rather than something emptied.']));

p('Brigid','Builder','Brigid organises building work, enjoys practical puzzles, and is determined that ordinary homes deserve good workmanship.',
 ['Well, that settles whether dragons are only old stories. I’m Brigid. Is he comfortable with people speaking to you?', 'Corin. This is Aurelius. Yes, you can speak to me; he knows we are meeting people.', 'Good. I would rather ask than conduct an entire conversation while pretending he was not there.'],
 'I’m Brigid. Building questions are welcome; complaints about builders may take a little longer.',
 'You and a dragon travelling together. I hope you find places that can make room for you both. Old stories rarely bother with that practical detail.',
 'Corin. How is the journey treating you?',
 t('What makes a house comfortable?', 'Somebody having asked the people who live there. I have seen handsome rooms that made every ordinary task awkward.',
 ['What do people forget most?', 'Where wet boots go. Grand plans are remarkably uninterested in mud.'],
 ['Can you fix a poor design?', 'Often, though asking first would have cost less than moving the doorway afterwards.'],
 ['Nan would have a long list of suggestions.', 'Then Nan is exactly who I would ask before drawing the room.']),
 t('Do you like puzzles?', 'The practical kind. Getting a large table through a small entrance makes people reveal a great deal about themselves.',
 ['How would you solve it?', 'Measure both before recruiting six neighbours to push. An unpopular opening move.'],
 ['Have you ever had to take a door off?', 'Several. I would rather remove a hinge deliberately than a doorframe accidentally.'],
 ['I would probably suggest pushing harder.', 'Most people do. Then one quiet person asks whether the legs come off.']),
 t('Could dragons and people share a town?', 'They would have to plan together. You cannot add a narrow little dragon corner and call the job finished.',
 ['Where would you begin?', 'With how a dragon moves, rests, and meets other people. We ought to ask the dragon.'],
 ['Would everything need rebuilding?', 'No. People often make room by using what they have more thoughtfully. Some new work would help.'],
 ['Aurelius might like having a place that fits.', 'Most of us do. He is entitled to that ordinary wish.']),
 t('Are the town’s repairs fairly shared?', 'The royal frontage receives fresh work while rented homes wait for basic repairs. A visitor sees the best wall and believes he has seen the town.',
 ['Who speaks for the tenants?', 'We try to make their complaints specific and public. A leaking room should not require a famous advocate.'],
 ['Could you just repair the homes first?', 'Sometimes we can. Other jobs are tied to orders and money we do not control.'],
 ['What should I notice when I visit a town?', 'How people live behind the impressive street. Ask before assuming the view tells you everything.']),
 t('What would you build with no deadline?', 'A schoolroom where nobody sits in the dark corner. I would spend an unreasonable amount of time watching where the light falls.',
 ['That seems a good use of time.', 'I think so. A child should not need the best seat to see the lesson.'],
 ['Would you make room for a dragon pupil?', 'If one wanted lessons. I would ask how large the pupil expected to become.'],
 ['Would you ever finish?', 'Eventually. I enjoy planning, but I enjoy watching people use a building more.']));

p('Tallis','Lutenist','A market musician who takes rehearsal seriously and his reputation less seriously than people expect.',
 ['I was about to ask what tune you wanted. Seeing your dragon has driven every tune out of my head. Tallis, usually a musician.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. We are happy to begin with a conversation while the tunes come back.', 'Merciful visitors. I shall remember that.'],
 'Tallis. Requests are welcome, though I reserve the right to admit I do not know them.',
 'A dragon companion? I have sung about riders for years. I had better start checking how much of it I invented.',
 'Corin! Conversation or music? Either makes a pleasant break from tuning.',
 t('How do you decide what to play?', 'I watch whether people are stopping to listen or simply trying to get their errands done. Those are different audiences.',
 ['Do you mind being background music?', 'Not at all. A market is allowed to remain a market while I enjoy myself.'],
 ['What if someone dislikes the tune?', 'They can request another. Shouting “something better” gives me very little to work with.'],
 ['Would you play something from Millwood?', 'If you can hum the beginning, I might know it under another name.']),
 t('Have you ever forgotten a song halfway through?', 'At a wedding. I repeated the same verse three times while trying to remember the next one.',
 ['Did the guests notice?', 'The bride joined in on the third repetition. She knew exactly what I was doing and rescued me.'],
 ['What did you do afterwards?', 'Thanked her. Then wrote the words somewhere I would actually look before performing.'],
 ['You could have called it a new arrangement.', 'I did. Nobody was obliged to believe me.']),
 t('Please do not turn us into a ballad yet.', 'Understood. I would rather hear your account than make you spend the next year correcting mine.',
 ['Most of it is less grand than people imagine.', 'So are most good stories. A missed turning can be more interesting than a foretold victory.'],
 ['Aurelius should have a say too.', 'Certainly. Two travellers, two accounts, and probably an argument about who was hungriest.'],
 ['Maybe when we have reached the end.', 'Then I will wait. You should have a chance to live the ending before I rhyme it.']),
 t('Are there songs you cannot play?', 'Yes. The crown dislikes a tune that lets a whole crowd agree on an unflattering opinion.',
 ['Does everyone know which songs?', 'Enough people do. The first few notes can change the mood of a street.'],
 ['Do you play them anyway?', 'I judge the company. An arrest would affect more people than the fellow holding the lute.'],
 ['Does that change how you write?', 'It makes me think about who bears the risk of a clever line.']),
 t('What do you want people to remember of your music?', 'An evening they were glad to have. I used to think it ought to be something much grander.',
 ['That seems enough to me.', 'It feels enough when someone tells me a tune helped them through a hard day.'],
 ['Have you stopped wanting applause?', 'Certainly not. I have become wiser, not mysteriously immune to applause.'],
 ['We could use an ordinary pleasant evening.', 'Then I shall resist writing an epic and find something you can hum on the road.']));

p('Tessa','Travelling flutist','Tessa performs in Forgewick and at Thornwell’s Copper Cup. Her gentle manner conceals very firm opinions about listening.',
 ['A dragon in the market. I nearly forgot to breathe, which is unfortunate for a flutist. I’m Tessa.', 'I’m Corin. This is Aurelius. Take your time; he has surprised quite a few people today.', 'Then I shall spare him another startled audience and say welcome.'],
 'Hello, I’m Tessa. I play here when I am not performing at the Copper Cup in Thornwell.',
 'A dragon travels with you? I hope he enjoys hearing new things as much as I do. You are both welcome to listen when I play.',
 'Hello again, Corin. Shall we give the music a rest and talk?',
 t('Why perform in more than one town?', 'A tune changes when different people sing along. I enjoy bringing it back with something I did not put there myself.',
 ['Does that happen between here and Thornwell?', 'Yes. The Copper Cup likes a lingering chorus. A market audience prefers you reach the interesting part before their errand is done.'],
 ['Do you get tired of travelling?', 'Sometimes. Then arriving among familiar people feels especially good.'],
 ['Would you rather settle in one place?', 'Perhaps one day. I am still curious about the next audience.']),
 t('What makes a good musical partner?', 'Tallis and I have learned to help each other recover from mistakes. Glaring to prove you heard one is not a useful musical contribution.',
 ['Do you and Tallis manage that?', 'Usually. We have both needed rescuing often enough to remember the arrangement.'],
 ['Can listeners tell?', 'Sometimes they think it was deliberate. We are happy to let them enjoy it.'],
 ['That sounds like travelling with someone.', 'I imagine it is. Keeping count of every mistake would make a long journey.']),
 t('Would music bother Aurelius?', 'I would rather you ask him than have me guess from whether he sits quietly. Quietness can mean several things.',
 ['I can ask what he enjoys.', 'Thank you. I would like an honest answer more than a polite audience.'],
 ['He might enjoy a tune from home.', 'If you remember one, I can try it. Familiar music need not sound exactly as it did the first time.'],
 ['We may just listen for a little while.', 'Then listen as long as you like, and leave when you need to.']),
 t('Does performing feel different under Halvard?', 'People check who is listening before they join certain songs. I miss hearing a room decide to sing without first making that calculation.',
 ['Do you blame them for being cautious?', 'No. A singer should not demand that an audience take risks to prove they enjoyed the music.'],
 ['Can an ordinary song still help?', 'Yes. Pleasure does not have to be a declaration to matter.'],
 ['What would you like to hear instead?', 'A crowd worrying about whether it knows the words, rather than whether it is allowed to know them.']),
 t('Have your travels changed what you want?', 'I used to collect new places as if the number mattered. Now I enjoy returning and noticing what I missed.',
 ['I am starting to understand that.', 'Somewhere becomes more interesting when you know a person there, not merely the way through.'],
 ['What do you notice on a return visit?', 'Who has learned a tune. Who wants to talk instead. Whether someone remembered me.'],
 ['You remembered us.', 'Of course. But I would like our second conversation even if the first had not involved a dragon.']));

p('Fara','Mender','Fara repairs clothing for working households and has a dry sense of humour about the excuses people bring with their torn sleeves.',
 ['Oh, those wings are real. I’m Fara. I hope my staring is not making your dragon uncomfortable.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. A hello is a good place to start. You need not pretend you see dragons every day.'],
 'I’m Fara. You look as though you have travelled a fair way. Come and catch your breath.',
 'A dragon! That is a travelling companion I have never had to mend a coat for. I hope the road is treating you both kindly.',
 'Hello, Corin. You need not bring something broken to stop for a chat.',
 t('What is the oddest repair you have done?', 'A man brought me a coat with every pocket torn. He had tried to carry a litter of kittens home in it.',
 ['Were the kittens all right?', 'Perfectly. His dignity took longer to mend than the coat.'],
 ['Did he explain why he had no basket?', 'At considerable length. I charged for the stitching, not the explanation.'],
 ['I can understand wanting to bring them home.', 'So could I. I put stronger pockets in, but advised a basket next time.']),
 t('How do you decide what is worth mending?', 'I ask what it means to its owner. A worn sleeve might matter more than the whole coat I would replace it with.',
 ['Do people tell you its story?', 'Often. They are relieved when I understand why they kept it.'],
 ['What if it really cannot be saved?', 'I say so gently. Sometimes a small piece can be kept even when the garment cannot.'],
 ['Nan keeps things from my parents.', 'Then let her tell you about them when she wants to. The story may be part of what she is keeping.']),
 t('Would you be afraid to meet Aurelius?', 'A little, probably. I would prefer to admit it than make him work out why I was smiling so stiffly.',
 ['He can give you some space.', 'Thank you. That sounds much better than being told I ought not to feel frightened.'],
 ['I was frightened when all this began.', 'I would have been too. It is good to know a friendship need not begin with perfect courage.'],
 ['There is no hurry.', 'Then I think we shall manage very well.']),
 t('Have you always lived in Forgewick?', 'I came here to help my sister for one winter. I made friends before I made plans to leave, and the plans never quite caught up.',
 ['Do you regret staying?', 'No. I do sometimes wonder about the other life I might have had. Wondering is not the same as wanting this one gone.'],
 ['Was it difficult being new?', 'Until someone remembered how I liked my tea. Such a small thing, but I felt less temporary.'],
 ['I miss knowing everyone.', 'You will find familiar people again. Give the new ones a little time.']),
 t('What would you like to hear about our journey?', 'Tell me about someone who was kind when you did not expect it. Those are the stories I like carrying into my own day.',
 ['I could ask Dunstan about our equipment.', 'He can sound brisk when he is being generous. I hope you told him it mattered.'],
 ['Some kindnesses seem too small for a story.', 'Those are often the ones I mean. A place to sit, a clear direction, someone waiting.'],
 ['I am still working out what to remember.', 'Then there is no need to give me the finished account today.']));

p('Garrick','Retired courier','Garrick carried messages between households and now takes an amused interest in the habits of travellers.',
 ['I thought I knew every sort of traveller. Evidently I had left dragons out. Garrick; formerly a courier.', 'I’m Corin. This is Aurelius. We are still learning how to be this sort of traveller ourselves.'],
 'Garrick. I used to carry messages; now I am content to hear the news without running anywhere.',
 'A dragon companion would have made my courier days memorable. I hope you are allowed to stop without somebody announcing an urgent errand.',
 'Corin, welcome. You look like someone who might appreciate a conversation with no delivery attached.',
 t('Did you ever deliver a message to the wrong person?', 'Once. Two cousins had the same name and each was convinced the invitation had been intended for him.',
 ['How did you sort it out?', 'Went back and asked the sender. Less dramatic than a quarrel, but more useful.'],
 ['Which cousin was invited?', 'Both, in the end. The host decided another supper was cheaper than a lasting feud.'],
 ['I would have been embarrassed.', 'I was. Correcting the mistake did more good than defending it.']),
 t('What made someone a good courier?', 'Remembering that the person waiting might care much more about the message than you understood.',
 ['Did you read the messages?', 'No. Their urgency did not make their contents my business.'],
 ['What if you arrived late?', 'I explained honestly. Inventing a heroic delay would not restore the lost time.'],
 ['Were there happy deliveries?', 'Births, reconciliations, invitations. I particularly liked the ones that made somebody sit down and smile.']),
 t('Would you have wanted a dragon to carry you?', 'As a young man, certainly. Now I would ask a great many questions about getting off again.',
 ['We could start with a very short trip.', 'Kind of you. I shall enjoy considering the offer before deciding whether my knees agree.'],
 ['Aurelius would have to agree as well.', 'Of course. A companion is not a faster hired horse.'],
 ['The view is wonderful.', 'Then keep looking at it. Speed can make people forget why they wanted to travel.']),
 t('Do you miss being expected somewhere?', 'Sometimes. Then a neighbour knocks just to ask how I am, and I remember that being wanted need not be a job.',
 ['Retiring must have been a change.', 'The first week I kept waking convinced I had forgotten a delivery.'],
 ['Have you found a new routine?', 'A walk when I choose, company when I can find it, and absolutely no sealed packets.'],
 ['I am always being sent somewhere lately.', 'I hope you also reach places where you can simply stay awhile.']),
 t('What would you tell a younger version of yourself?', 'Not every delay is a failure. I passed some lovely places without stopping because I wanted to arrive impressively early.',
 ['Did anyone appreciate the early arrivals?', 'A few. Others had to get out of bed, and were considerably less impressed.'],
 ['I am worried about wasting time.', 'Understandable. Resting enough to think clearly is rarely wasted time.'],
 ['Would you change much?', 'A few hurried goodbyes. I cannot change those, but I can be less hurried now.']));

p('Junia','Amateur storyteller','Junia writes short comic stories for friends and is learning to finish them before inventing better beginnings.',
 ['There is a dragon with you. I have spent years inventing unlikely visitors and now feel rather unimaginative. I’m Junia.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius. I promise we did not arrive to criticise your stories.'],
 'Hello, I’m Junia. If you have come with a story, I shall try very hard not to interrupt.',
 'You travel with a dragon? Then I will ask before borrowing anything from your life. It is quite different when the person can object.',
 'Corin, hello. I have resisted turning your last visit into fiction.',
 t('What sort of stories do you write?', 'Small disasters that end with supper. I like giving my characters something pleasant after making their day difficult.',
 ['Do they deserve the supper?', 'Even the foolish ones. Especially the foolish ones, sometimes.'],
 ['Why small disasters?', 'I understand a ruined cake better than a kingdom. There is enough drama in either if somebody cares.'],
 ['Have you finished many?', 'Fewer than I have begun. I am trying to make that less of a defining trait.']),
 t('Who reads your stories?', 'A few friends. One laughs at everything, and another tells me when she has lost track of who is speaking.',
 ['Which is more helpful?', 'Both, on different days. Encouragement gets me writing; a clear question gets me revising.'],
 ['Do you mind criticism?', 'I mind for a minute. Then I decide whether it helps. I am improving at not making the minute somebody else’s problem.'],
 ['What if a reader misunderstands?', 'I look at what I wrote before explaining what I meant. The words have to do the work when I am not there.']),
 t('Would you write Aurelius as a villain?', 'Not because he is a dragon. That would tell the reader almost nothing about him and rather a lot about my laziness.',
 ['He does have opinions about stories.', 'Excellent. I am prepared to hear them, including the inconvenient ones.'],
 ['What would make a good dragon character?', 'A desire that matters to him, and choices that reveal more than the size of his teeth.'],
 ['We are not sure how our story ends.', 'Then I will not spoil it by deciding for you.']),
 t('Do people in Forgewick like stories?', 'Very much. They simply insist the best ones happened to a cousin and therefore do not count as fiction.',
 ['Do you believe them?', 'I believe there was probably a cousin. Beyond that, I admire the performance.'],
 ['Can you tell when a story has travelled?', 'Details become grander while the directions become less reliable.'],
 ['I would like people to remember what really happened.', 'Then keep your own account. A modest truthful detail can survive beside a spectacular rumour.']),
 t('Have you finished a story since we spoke?', 'Yes. I let the ending be quiet instead of trying to make every character deliver a magnificent final sentence.',
 ['What happens?', 'They mend the friendship, eat the supper, and leave the washing until morning.'],
 ['Are you pleased with it?', 'I am. There are things I would change, but finished is a useful place to stand while deciding.'],
 ['That sounds like an ending I would enjoy.', 'Then perhaps I have finally written one for somebody besides myself.']));

p('Kellan','Apprentice toolmaker','Kellan is precise at work, inventive with games, and much less confident than his cheerful explanations suggest.',
 ['I’m Kellan. I would normally offer my hand, but I am not sure how to greet your dragon.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. Saying hello is fine. We are not expecting a special ceremony.'],
 'Kellan. I make tools, or help make them, depending on how generous my teacher feels that day.',
 'A dragon on your travels. I hope you do not mind questions; I have several, though I can choose just one at a time.',
 'Hello again, Corin. I promise I have not saved every question since your last visit.',
 t('What are you learning to make?', 'Tools that feel right in the hand. I thought matching the shape would be enough until someone actually used my first attempt.',
 ['What was wrong with it?', 'The balance. It looked handsome and made a wrist ache within minutes.'],
 ['Could you fix it?', 'Yes. The owner showed me instead of merely telling me it was bad.'],
 ['That must have been disappointing.', 'It was useful disappointment. I know what to pay attention to now.']),
 t('What games do you like?', 'Ones where a clever move can rescue a poor beginning. I prefer that to losing because the dice disliked me at breakfast.',
 ['Do you invent your own?', 'Frequently. My family requests fewer rules and shorter explanations.'],
 ['Would you let a beginner win?', 'I would help them understand. Pretending they had won seems a rather disappointing gift.'],
 ['I like a little luck.', 'So do I, provided it remembers to visit both players.']),
 t('Could Aurelius use tools?', 'I do not know what he would want one for. Asking that would be more useful than making a large human tool and congratulating myself.',
 ['He might prefer doing things his own way.', 'Then I would learn something by watching, if he agreed.'],
 ['Would you enjoy designing something for him?', 'Very much. A problem with a real person behind it is the best kind to solve.'],
 ['He is cleverer than people expect.', 'People might begin by expecting more. It would save everyone time.']),
 t('Do you want your own workshop?', 'Eventually. I would like to become reliable before I become responsible for somebody else’s learning.',
 ['What kind of teacher would you be?', 'One who remembers that “obvious” usually means “I have done this before”.'],
 ['Are you in a hurry?', 'Some days. Then I look at a piece I made last year and feel less certain that haste is my friend.'],
 ['Would you stay in Forgewick?', 'I think so. It would be satisfying to make a place for myself here.']),
 t('Are you feeling more confident?', 'Enough to admit when I do not know. It turns out that concealing a question takes more effort than asking it.',
 ['I still find that difficult.', 'So do I. I have not become a different person; I have acquired a useful habit.'],
 ['Has anyone noticed?', 'My teacher says I waste less metal. It is an affectionate compliment, by his standards.'],
 ['What are you proud of lately?', 'A repair nobody noticed because it worked. I am learning to enjoy that kind of success.']));

p('Lysa','Weaver','Lysa values sturdy cloth, exuberant colours, and gifts chosen for the person who will receive them.',
 ['A dragon! I’m Lysa. Please tell me I have not frightened him by exclaiming like that.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. You surprised me more than him. We are both all right.', 'Then welcome. I shall attempt a quieter second impression.'],
 'I’m Lysa. Come in, if you have a moment. I enjoy hearing where people have been.',
 'You have a dragon companion? I should like to meet him, though I may need a moment to believe my eyes when I do.',
 'Corin, hello. How are you and Aurelius managing?',
 t('How do you choose colours?', 'I ask what someone likes before asking what room the cloth belongs in. They have to live with it longer than their visitors do.',
 ['What if they choose something very bright?', 'Then I try to make it a good bright cloth. My task is not to make everyone share my taste.'],
 ['What colours would you choose for yourself?', 'Green and a particularly cheerful yellow. Nobody has ever accused the combination of being discreet.'],
 ['Nan would choose something that hides stains.', 'A fine practical beginning. There is usually room for beauty after that.']),
 t('Are you good at choosing gifts?', 'I once gave a friend a beautiful sewing basket. She had been trying to tell everyone how much she disliked sewing.',
 ['What did she say?', 'Thank you, very kindly. I understood the mistake much later and apologised.'],
 ['What would you give her now?', 'An afternoon out together. Something she actually enjoys.'],
 ['At least you meant well.', 'I did. Listening would have made the good intention more useful.']),
 t('Do you think dragons like beautiful things?', 'I cannot see why they would all like the same things. People keep asking what dragons prefer as if one answer should do for everyone.',
 ['Aurelius has his own favourites.', 'Then I would enjoy learning one of his, if he wanted to tell me.'],
 ['He notices things I walk past.', 'A good travelling companion can lend you another way of seeing.'],
 ['I wish people asked him more often.', 'You may count me among those willing to learn how.']),
 t('What do you like about living here?', 'There are people I can disagree with and still visit the next day. That seems a valuable sort of neighbourhood.',
 ['Does that happen often?', 'Often enough. A discussion about curtains once lasted three visits, and nobody bought any curtains.'],
 ['What keeps it friendly?', 'Remembering that winning a small argument is not worth losing a pleasant neighbour.'],
 ['I miss familiar company.', 'You are welcome to become familiar company here too.']),
 t('Would you travel if you had the chance?', 'Yes, but slowly. I would like to spend enough time somewhere to learn more than the road out.',
 ['Where would you begin?', 'Sandspire. The colours people describe sound like something I ought to see for myself.'],
 ['Would you bring work?', 'One small piece. I enjoy having something familiar in my hands while everything else is new.'],
 ['Perhaps our paths will cross.', 'I would like that. Then you could ask whether I finally learned to pack lightly.']));

p('Cinder','Former forge tender','Cinder enjoys hearty cooking and quiet company after years of tending demanding fires.',
 ['A dragon at my door. Well, I shall not pretend that was on my list of expected visitors. Cinder is my name.', 'I’m Corin, and this is Aurelius. We hope we are welcome despite the surprise.', 'You are. An unexpected guest can still be a welcome one.'],
 'Cinder. Have you come far? I am better company once I know whether someone needs directions or a rest.',
 'Travelling with a dragon must change what you consider an ordinary day. You are welcome to tell me about him.',
 'Corin, hello. I am glad you stopped again.',
 t('Do you enjoy cooking?', 'I enjoy feeding people. The cooking sometimes argues with that ambition, particularly when I decide not to measure anything.',
 ['What goes wrong?', 'Usually the amount. I can feed four people or fourteen; I struggle with every number between.'],
 ['What do you like making?', 'A thick stew that forgives being kept warm while someone is late.'],
 ['That sounds like Nan’s kind of meal.', 'Then Nan and I would probably spend supper agreeing and the washing-up disagreeing.']),
 t('Was tending a forge difficult?', 'You had to notice a change before it became a problem. People think the loudest person must be doing the most important work.',
 ['Were you quiet?', 'At work, yes. At cards, my friends might give you another answer.'],
 ['How did you learn to notice?', 'Someone patient made me explain what I was seeing instead of guessing what he wanted to hear.'],
 ['Do you still miss it?', 'Parts of it. I do not miss being too tired to enjoy the evening.']),
 t('Does dragon fire interest you?', 'Certainly. But I do not intend to greet Aurelius by asking him to light something. He has not come here seeking employment.',
 ['People do seem to think of jobs for him.', 'Then he will appreciate the occasional person who simply wants his company.'],
 ['He might show you if he wanted.', 'And I would be impressed. The wanting is the important part.'],
 ['I am still getting used to it myself.', 'You are allowed to be amazed by your own life now and then.']),
 t('Do you prefer company or quiet?', 'Company that does not fear a quiet moment. Nobody should have to talk without stopping to prove they are enjoying a visit.',
 ['I sometimes struggle to find the next thing to say.', 'Then we can let the last thing settle. It will not be offended.'],
 ['Were your workmates like that?', 'Some. Shared work gave us things to discuss and the good sense to stop discussing them.'],
 ['That sounds restful.', 'It is. A visitor should not leave needing to recover from the visit.']),
 t('What would make a good day now?', 'A useful task in the morning, a meal with somebody I like, and nothing urgent invented at dusk.',
 ['A modest wish.', 'A carefully tested one. Grand ambitions kept changing; this has lasted.'],
 ['Would a dragon at supper spoil the quiet?', 'An invited dragon would be company. An urgent royal inspection would spoil it.'],
 ['I hope we get days like that.', 'I hope you recognise them when you do. They are easy to overlook while waiting for something grand.']));

p('Warden','Neighbourhood organiser','Warden arranges help between mining households and fiercely protects the distinction between a favour and a debt.',
 ['I’m Warden. I was going to ask whether you needed help, but I must first ask about the dragon.', 'Corin. His name is Aurelius; we travel together. We do not need rescuing, but a welcome would be nice.', 'That I can provide. Welcome, both of you.'],
 'I’m Warden. Is somebody expecting you, or are you finding your way around?',
 'A dragon companion. I hope people are remembering to ask how you both are, as well as how you came to meet.',
 'Hello, Corin. You may visit without bringing a problem to solve.',
 t('What do you organise for your neighbours?', 'Meals when someone is ill, a repair when somebody cannot manage it, company when a house has become too quiet.',
 ['Does everyone contribute?', 'In different ways. I do not measure an old neighbour’s company against a strong neighbour’s lifting.'],
 ['Do you keep a list of favours?', 'Only of what needs doing. A kindness should not arrive carrying a bill for later.'],
 ['Do you get any rest yourself?', 'I am learning to accept the same advice I give everyone else.']),
 t('Does your husband work in the mines?', 'Yes. He tells me the cheerful parts first, which would be more convincing if I had not known him so long.',
 ['Does he tell you the rest eventually?', 'Usually. I prefer an honest difficult day to a brave little performance over supper.'],
 ['Do you worry when he is late?', 'Of course. Knowing a trade is dangerous does not make waiting easier.'],
 ['What do you enjoy doing together?', 'Walking without any particular destination. He says it is a pleasure to choose which way to go.']),
 t('What help would you offer a dragon?', 'I would ask him. People offer the help they enjoy giving and sometimes forget to check whether it is needed.',
 ['Space to rest would help us both.', 'That is a sensible thing to ask for. You need not turn it into a grand explanation.'],
 ['He might just like being included.', 'Then I shall remember to speak about both of you without making him the subject of every sentence.'],
 ['I am not always sure what I need either.', 'Then start with what is making the day harder. That can be easier to name.']),
 t('What is difficult about organising people?', 'Persuading capable people that accepting help does not cancel all the help they have given.',
 ['I struggle with that.', 'Most of us do. Try imagining how pleased you are when someone lets you be useful.'],
 ['What if I cannot repay it?', 'Then be honest and accept what is freely offered. Repayment was not the question.'],
 ['Have you learned to accept it?', 'Better than I used to. My neighbours are persistent, which serves me right.']),
 t('What should we do when the journey feels too much?', 'Tell each other before exhaustion turns every small decision into an argument.',
 ['We are trying to look after each other.', 'That includes saying when you need looking after. It can be harder than offering.'],
 ['What if we need different things?', 'Then say so. A compromise works better when neither person has to guess the other’s problem.'],
 ['I am glad we stopped to talk.', 'So am I. Not every useful stop has to give you an item for your bag.']));

p('Ember','Home baker','Ember likes bold flavours and has strong, occasionally impractical opinions about celebrations.',
 ['A dragon! I’m Ember. Yes, that really is my name. I promise I did not choose it to impress him.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. I think an ordinary welcome will impress him more than a clever name.'],
 'I’m Ember. If you have come to settle an argument about food, I hope you agree with me.',
 'You travel with a dragon? Then I had better ask about his food instead of assuming anything with my name must interest him.',
 'Corin, welcome back. Shall we discuss something more cheerful than the state of the roads?',
 t('What makes a proper celebration?', 'A reason people understand and food they actually want to eat. Dagna says I forget the part about who will wash the dishes.',
 ['Who does wash them?', 'We both do. I complain extravagantly and then get on with it.'],
 ['Does it need to be a big occasion?', 'Not at all. A friend returning is an excellent excuse.'],
 ['I would like one without a speech.', 'So would I. The food gets cold while somebody explains why we are happy.']),
 t('Do you invent recipes?', 'With mixed results. I once improved a perfectly good loaf so thoroughly that nobody would finish it.',
 ['What did you add?', 'Three things that would each have been pleasant on their own. I mistook enthusiasm for judgement.'],
 ['Did you try again?', 'Yes. With fewer improvements. The second loaf was eaten, which I took as a review.'],
 ['I like simple food after travelling.', 'Then tell the cook. Hungry people need not admire an experiment.']),
 t('Would you cook for Aurelius?', 'If I knew what he liked. A thoughtful meal begins with the guest, not with the cook’s exciting idea.',
 ['Meat and fish are useful provisions for him.', 'Then I shall remember that instead of planning a ceremonial dragon cake.'],
 ['He would enjoy being asked.', 'So would anyone. Famous guests ought to retain ordinary preferences.'],
 ['He might appreciate the dragon cake too.', 'Now you are encouraging me. Dagna will want your name when this becomes a project.']),
 t('Do you and Dagna agree on anything?', 'Almost everything important. That leaves us free to argue magnificently about supper.',
 ['Does one of you usually win?', 'We usually end up eating. I consider that a joint victory.'],
 ['Can you tell when an argument matters?', 'Yes. Then I stop trying to be funny and listen.'],
 ['I like hearing people comfortable together.', 'It takes practice. Knowing someone well is a reason to be careful with them, not careless.']),
 t('What would you celebrate for us?', 'Getting a little time in which nobody needs rescuing. I suspect you could both use that.',
 ['We certainly could.', 'Then let that be enough reason. You need not defeat something every time you want a pleasant evening.'],
 ['Aurelius might prefer a quiet meal.', 'Then it would be a quiet celebration. I can be instructed, despite what Dagna says.'],
 ['I would invite the people who helped us.', 'Good. Tell them why you wanted them there before the evening is over.']));

p('Dagna','Launderer','Dagna enjoys blunt conversation, well-kept promises, and surprising people with a competitive streak.',
 ['I’m Dagna. I was prepared for a visitor, but not for a dragon looking back at me.', 'I’m Corin; he is Aurelius. We can give you a little room if you need it.', 'Thank you. A moment to collect myself will do.'],
 'Dagna. Come and say what is on your mind; I prefer that to guessing.',
 'A dragon travelling with you? I imagine you have heard every possible exclamation already. Let me offer a plain welcome instead.',
 'Hello, Corin. Good to see you under your own steam.',
 t('What do people misunderstand about your work?', 'That clean clothes happen by themselves if you leave them with somebody long enough.',
 ['Do people forget to thank you?', 'Sometimes. More often they forget how long the work takes.'],
 ['What would make it easier?', 'Being told about a stain before it has been rubbed in by someone’s hopeful experiment.'],
 ['I am afraid travelling is hard on clothes.', 'Clothes are meant to be lived in. I object more to careless explanations than honest wear.']),
 t('Are you competitive?', 'Only at games I claim not to care about. Ember has become very good at recognising the phrase.',
 ['What gives you away?', 'I ask to see the rules immediately after losing.'],
 ['Do you ever play just for fun?', 'It is fun. I merely enjoy the winning part a great deal.'],
 ['Would you teach me a game?', 'Gladly. I would explain the rules before trying to exploit them.']),
 t('Would you be comfortable around Aurelius?', 'I think so, once I knew how to avoid bothering him. I dislike being told someone is harmless when what I asked was how to be polite.',
 ['Ask before touching him.', 'That seems a very reasonable beginning. People should manage it without special training.'],
 ['Give his wings room when he moves.', 'Of course. I would rather shift myself than make him fold up for everyone else.'],
 ['He can let me know if he is uncomfortable.', 'Then I will listen when you tell me.']),
 t('Do you enjoy living with Ember?', 'Yes. Ember makes a dull day more interesting. I make an interesting plan slightly more possible.',
 ['That sounds like a good partnership.', 'When we remember to discuss the plan before inviting people.'],
 ['Do you ever want a quieter evening?', 'Certainly. I say so, and the world somehow survives.'],
 ['What does Ember appreciate about you?', 'My patience, allegedly. I suspect my ability to find things is higher on the list.']),
 t('Have you heard any rumours about us?', 'Enough to know I would rather ask you. Rumours keep improving a story until nobody involved recognises it.',
 ['Thank you for not repeating them as facts.', 'You are welcome. It costs me nothing to admit I was not there.'],
 ['Were any of them amusing?', 'A few. I have resisted checking whether Aurelius can count the money in a purse by smelling it.'],
 ['He cannot.', 'Then another extraordinary business opportunity is lost to us.']));

p('Lode','Retired miner','Lode remembers difficult shifts clearly, but would rather be known for his cooking and terrible guesses at riddles.',
 ['I’m Lode. I have mistaken plenty of things for dragons in the dark. This is the first one to arrive with a visitor.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius, and I can confirm you are seeing him properly.'],
 'Lode. Come closer if you want to talk; there is no need to shout a conversation across a room.',
 'A dragon companion. I shall have to stop dismissing every surprising report as a tired miner’s imagination.',
 'Corin, hello. Tell me you have stopped for something other than advice about holes in the ground.',
 t('Are you good at riddles?', 'Appalling. I always suspect the sensible answer is a trap and choose something elaborate and wrong.',
 ['Give me an example.', 'Someone asked what gets wetter as it dries. I proposed an underground river. Apparently it was a towel.'],
 ['Perhaps the elaborate answer was better.', 'Thank you. I shall cite your support at the next humiliating supper.'],
 ['Do you still enjoy them?', 'Certainly. My friends enjoy them even more when I am present.']),
 t('What did you listen for underground?', 'Anything that changed. You learn the familiar sounds so an unfamiliar one has a chance to catch your attention.',
 ['Could you tell if something was dangerous?', 'Sometimes. Sometimes you stopped work and found out. Guessing confidently was not a skill I admired.'],
 ['Did you ever ignore a warning?', 'Once, and someone wiser stopped me. I remember him more clearly than the argument.'],
 ['That sounds tiring.', 'It could be. Coming into daylight did more than let you see the sky.']),
 t('Did you ever dream of flying?', 'Often, after a long shift. In my dreams I was excellent at it and needed no explanation of how to land.',
 ['Landing does take some care.', 'An unfortunate detail. Dreams are poor instruction manuals.'],
 ['Would you like to try with Aurelius?', 'I would like to think about trying. Let me enjoy that stage before you ask for a decision.'],
 ['He loves having room above him.', 'I can understand that without having wings myself.']),
 t('What do you like to cook?', 'Soup. A forgiving meal, provided you know when to stop adding things.',
 ['Do you know when to stop?', 'More often now. I have served some very determined soups.'],
 ['What makes a good one?', 'Enough time, decent ingredients, and remembering who will have to eat it.'],
 ['Does it remind you of work?', 'No. That is among its finest qualities.']),
 t('What would you like to do next?', 'Visit somewhere without learning its mining history. I intend to disappoint every guide who offers it.',
 ['The sea might suit you.', 'It might. I should like a horizon that makes no suggestion of being excavated.'],
 ['Would you go alone?', 'No. Someone should be there to laugh when I misunderstand the local riddles.'],
 ['I hope you make the trip.', 'So do I. Saying it aloud makes it harder to postpone indefinitely.']));

p('Pike','Basket maker','Pike makes durable baskets, knows the cost of a mining shift to a household, and enjoys sharp bargains.',
 ['I’m Pike. Is your dragon here for a visit too, or should I stop staring and let you ask for directions?', 'Corin, and Aurelius. A visit, if you have time. He is getting to know people as well.', 'Then a visit it is. I can spare the time.'],
 'Pike. A traveller, by the look of you. What would you like to know?',
 'You and a dragon on the road. I imagine that makes packing for the journey an interesting calculation.',
 'Hello, Corin. What have you discovered since we last spoke?',
 t('How do you know a basket will last?', 'Fill it and carry it. A basket that only behaves while empty is an ornament with ambitions.',
 ['Do customers ever bring one back?', 'Yes. I would rather know what failed than have them quietly decide I make bad work.'],
 ['What is hardest to carry?', 'Something that keeps moving. My most demanding customer was a goose.'],
 ['Did the goose approve?', 'It objected to the entire arrangement. I did not take that personally.']),
 t('Do you enjoy bargaining?', 'Yes, when both people can walk away. It stops being a game when one person has no choice.',
 ['Do you always get the lower price?', 'No. Sometimes I discover why the higher one was fair.'],
 ['How do I avoid being cheated?', 'Ask what you are buying and what it does. Anyone annoyed by a reasonable question is giving you useful information.'],
 ['I feel awkward asking.', 'You are discussing your own money. You have a place in the conversation.']),
 t('How much should we carry for Aurelius?', 'Enough for a sensible journey, not so much that looking after tomorrow exhausts you today. Ask a provisions seller about what you actually use.',
 ['Toft can show us his stock.', 'Yes. He understands the difference between a helpful supply and a heavy purchase.'],
 ['Aurelius gets hungry rather often.', 'Growing creatures do. Remember your own meals while planning his.'],
 ['We can hunt, and fishing might help too.', 'Then leave room for what you find. A full bag can be surprisingly inconvenient.']),
 t('Does your husband enjoy mining?', 'Some parts. He likes the people and takes pride in doing the work well. That does not mean he enjoys every shift.',
 ['Does he talk about it at home?', 'When he wants to. We have other subjects, believe it or not.'],
 ['What do you talk about instead?', 'Food, neighbours, where we might go on a free day. Ordinary things worth getting home for.'],
 ['I did not mean to make it his whole life.', 'I know. People ask because they are interested. I am fond of reminding them there is more.']),
 t('What would you pack for a holiday?', 'Half what I packed for the last one. I took enough spare clothing to establish a second household.',
 ['Did you use any of it?', 'One extra pair of socks. The socks had an excellent holiday; the rest saw the inside of a bag.'],
 ['Would your husband pack more sensibly?', 'He would claim so until he had to borrow something from my bag.'],
 ['I will try to remember the socks.', 'Good. Practical wisdom rarely sounds grand when you finally say it.']));

p('Hallow','Repairer','Hallow takes pleasure in ingenious repairs and has an unreasonable affection for mechanisms that nobody else wants to mend.',
 ['A dragon, quite plainly. I’m Hallow. I was about to offer a clever explanation for what I was seeing, but that would be a poor introduction.', 'Corin. His name is Aurelius. The plain explanation is the right one this time.'],
 'Hallow. Tell me what you are wondering, and I will tell you if I know anything useful.',
 'A dragon travels with you? I admire a fact that refuses to fit the explanation somebody prepared for it.',
 'Corin, hello. What puzzle have you brought me today?',
 t('Will you repair absolutely anything?', 'I once accepted a clock that had already been repaired by three people. Each had left an extra part inside.',
 ['Did you get it working?', 'Eventually. I had to undo the improvements before addressing the original problem.'],
 ['Why not refuse it?', 'Because it was interesting, which is how I get into most difficulties.'],
 ['Did the owner appreciate it?', 'Very much. He said it had not told the same time twice for years.']),
 t('How do you work out what is broken?', 'First I ask what happened just before it stopped working. People like to begin with their theory instead.',
 ['Do you listen to the theory too?', 'Yes. Occasionally it is right, and it is always important to the person telling it.'],
 ['What if they cannot remember?', 'Then we inspect it carefully. Not knowing is an ordinary part of finding out.'],
 ['I tend to poke things until they work.', 'A popular method. It creates a great deal of employment for me.']),
 t('Are you trying to work out how Aurelius flies?', 'I am curious, but he does not owe me an explanation. A living creature is a poor thing to mistake for an interesting mechanism.',
 ['He might enjoy your questions.', 'Then I shall begin with one and see whether he wants another.'],
 ['I mostly trust that he knows how.', 'A sensible arrangement. You need not understand every motion to trust your companion.'],
 ['I would enjoy learning more myself.', 'Ask him about what it feels like first. That answer belongs to him.']),
 t('Have you ever made a problem worse?', 'Several. The most expensive began with “this will only take a moment”. I now try to leave that phrase out of my estimates.',
 ['Did you admit it?', 'I had to. The customer could see the extra pieces.'],
 ['What did you learn?', 'To stop when my first guess fails, rather than making three more repairs to defend it.'],
 ['That sounds familiar.', 'Then we may both become wiser without having to repeat every mistake ourselves.']),
 t('What would you mend if time were no object?', 'An old music box I have at home. Its owner died before I could finish it. Her daughter said there was no hurry.',
 ['Do you want to give it to her?', 'Yes. She ought to hear the tune properly once, if I can manage it.'],
 ['Is it very difficult?', 'The last part is. I am making it carefully instead of promising a date I cannot keep.'],
 ['I hope you finish it.', 'So do I. Some jobs deserve patience without being forgotten.']));

p('Quarrel','Opinionated neighbour','Quarrel objects to careless thinking, enjoys being contradicted well, and occasionally forgets to sound as friendly as intended.',
 ['Before you ask, Quarrel is my name, not an invitation. And before I ask anything else: is that a dragon?', 'Corin. Yes, this is Aurelius. I hope we can manage an introduction without living up to your name.', 'A reasonable proposal. Welcome.'],
 'Quarrel. Yes, that is my name. You may get the inevitable question over with.',
 'You travel with a dragon? Then I withdraw several confident remarks I have made about what travellers exaggerate.',
 'Corin. Come and give me something interesting to disagree with.',
 t('Do you enjoy arguing?', 'I enjoy an argument that changes somebody’s mind. Two people repeating themselves is merely noise with an audience.',
 ['Does your mind ever change?', 'Annoyingly often. I try to announce it clearly enough to spare everyone a second argument.'],
 ['What makes a good argument?', 'Knowing what the other person actually said. A surprisingly neglected beginning.'],
 ['I would rather avoid a quarrel.', 'Then we can agree about lunch. I contain multitudes.']),
 t('Has your name caused trouble?', 'People assume I am angry before I begin. Occasionally that is useful; usually it is a nuisance.',
 ['Have you considered a nickname?', 'Flint proposed “Sunshine”. I declined.'],
 ['Were you named after somebody?', 'A relative with a perfectly respectable name and an entirely unreasonable spelling. Families are mysterious.'],
 ['I will try to judge you by what you say.', 'Dangerous, but fair. I accept the terms.']),
 t('Do you believe us about Aurelius?', 'I believe there is a dragon. What I will not do is conclude that every story ever told about dragons must therefore be true.',
 ['That seems sensible.', 'Thank you. I was prepared to defend it at unnecessary length.'],
 ['Some stories make him uncomfortable.', 'Then people should stop using them as introductions.'],
 ['You could ask him what he thinks.', 'With your help, gladly. An actual answer would improve several local debates.']),
 t('Can you disagree with a friend?', 'Of course. The difficulty is remembering that the friendship still matters when you have found a magnificent reply.',
 ['Have you ever regretted saying it?', 'Yes. Wit does not mend the harm merely because everyone else laughed.'],
 ['Do you apologise?', 'When I have been unkind. It would be a poor argument to insist my pride mattered more than the person.'],
 ['What does Flint think?', 'That I explain my apologies at excessive length. He may have a point.']),
 t('Have you changed your opinion of us?', 'I have acquired an opinion. At first you were two strangers surrounded by other people’s expectations.',
 ['And now?', 'You ask questions and you return to hear the answers. I approve, though you need not make a ceremony of it.'],
 ['Are we allowed to disappoint you?', 'Certainly. Approval that depends on perfection is a tiresome sort of trap.'],
 ['That almost sounded affectionate.', 'Then I must have expressed myself unusually clearly.']));

p('Flint','Retired kiln worker','Flint enjoys harmless mischief, practical jokes with fair endings, and keeping Quarrel from taking every conversation too seriously.',
 ['I’m Flint. I was about to tell you Quarrel bites, but your dragon rather changes the joke.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. Perhaps we should start with everyone agreeing not to bite anyone.', 'An excellent local custom. I support it.'],
 'Flint. Have you come for a serious conversation? I can attempt one if warned.',
 'A dragon companion. Quarrel will have to revise several opinions. I look forward to the announcement.',
 'Corin! A welcome interruption. I was in danger of becoming industrious.',
 t('What is a good practical joke?', 'One the victim can enjoy once it is explained. Otherwise you have merely found an audience for being unpleasant.',
 ['Have your jokes always managed that?', 'No. I learned the rule by getting it wrong and apologising.'],
 ['What does Quarrel find funny?', 'Me being caught in a joke I arranged. He has very dependable taste.'],
 ['I prefer knowing what is happening.', 'Then I will leave you out of the surprises. Knowing the audience is part of the job.']),
 t('Did you enjoy working at the kiln?', 'I enjoyed the people. We had arguments about everything except whether we wanted everyone home at the end of the day.',
 ['Did you stay friends?', 'With some. Work puts people together; friendship takes a little attention after that.'],
 ['What did you argue about?', 'Recipes, weather, whose turn it was to fetch something. Grand subjects, passionately handled.'],
 ['Do you miss the routine?', 'Sometimes. Then I enjoy sleeping a little longer and recover.']),
 t('Would you play a joke on Aurelius?', 'Only if I knew he would enjoy it. Being different from me is not an invitation to become the joke.',
 ['He has a sense of humour.', 'Then I should enjoy meeting it, rather than testing his patience.'],
 ['He might get you back.', 'As he should. A joke with no right of reply is poor sport.'],
 ['Perhaps start with a story.', 'A wise proposal. I have several in which I am the fool.']),
 t('How do you put up with Quarrel?', 'With affection and occasional strategic deafness. He puts up with me by insisting it builds character.',
 ['Do you take his advice?', 'Often. I simply refuse to look impressed every time he is right.'],
 ['Does he know you appreciate him?', 'Yes. I make sure the teasing does not have to carry that message by itself.'],
 ['You sound happy together.', 'Most days. Happiness is allowed to include a disagreement about whose turn it is.']),
 t('What story would you tell about our visit?', 'That a dragonrider came to talk and stayed long enough for us to stop making a fuss about the dragonrider.',
 ['I like that version.', 'So do I. People are more interesting once you let them stop making an entrance.'],
 ['Would Aurelius get his own part?', 'Certainly. I have been listening when you say there are two of you.'],
 ['Please leave out anything embarrassing.', 'I shall apply the same generous editing I request for my own life.']));

p('Bors','Household carpenter','Bors makes practical furniture, cherishes his husband, and believes a useful object should survive ordinary clumsiness.',
 ['I’m Bors. Your companion is a dragon, and I am going to need a better greeting than the noise I nearly made.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius. We can give you a moment; it has been a surprising journey for us too.'],
 'Bors. You are welcome to stop and talk, provided you do not need a brilliant answer immediately.',
 'A dragon travels with you? I hope the two of you have somewhere comfortable to return to. A road is a fine thing until you need a home.',
 'Corin, hello. I am pleased you found time for another visit.',
 t('What furniture do you like making?', 'Chairs for people who actually sit in them. I distrust a chair that makes its owner apologise for being comfortable.',
 ['What makes a bad chair?', 'A lovely shape in all the wrong places. Your back discovers the fault much faster than your eyes.'],
 ['Do people choose appearance over comfort?', 'Often. Then they ask for a cushion and blame themselves.'],
 ['Nan has a favourite chair.', 'Then somebody got something right, even if they never received a compliment for it.']),
 t('How did you meet your husband?', 'He came to collect a repaired stool and stayed to discuss everything except the stool.',
 ['Did you realise why?', 'Not immediately. I gave him a very thorough account of the repair. He has never let me forget it.'],
 ['What made you notice?', 'He came back the next week without anything broken. I finally caught up.'],
 ['That is a lovely beginning.', 'I think so. It improved considerably once I stopped discussing joinery.']),
 t('Does travelling with a dragon seem strange to you?', 'Unexpected, yes. Two people finding that they are better together is easier to understand.',
 ['It has happened rather quickly.', 'Then give yourselves room to keep learning. A strong beginning need not do the work of every later day.'],
 ['We do not always understand each other.', 'Neither do my husband and I. Asking is usually kinder than assuming.'],
 ['I am glad someone sees it that way.', 'I would rather welcome the friendship than spend the whole visit astonished by its shape.']),
 t('Do you make things for your own home?', 'Usually after promising myself I will. I can finish a neighbour’s shelf in a day and postpone my own for a season.',
 ['Why is that?', 'A neighbour comes to collect it. My own shelf has not learned to knock.'],
 ['Does your husband remind you?', 'With increasing artistry. The requests have become a little performance.'],
 ['Perhaps choose a day for it.', 'That is annoyingly sensible. I may have to do it now you have said it.']),
 t('Did you finish your own shelf?', 'Yes. My husband admired it, then immediately found something else I had promised to mend.',
 ['Was it worth doing?', 'Very much. I had forgotten how pleasant it is to enjoy my own work at home.'],
 ['Have you learned your lesson?', 'Let us say I have begun learning it. That leaves room for the next overdue repair.'],
 ['You both sound pleased.', 'We are. Domestic triumph rarely looks impressive from the road, but it counts.']));

p('Kiln','Potter','Kiln makes tableware and enjoys the stubborn individuality of handmade objects.',
 ['I’m Kiln. I have made little clay dragons, but never expected to be judged by a living one.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. He is here to meet people, not inspect your pottery.'],
 'Kiln. Come and tell me what you have been seeing on the road.',
 'A dragon as a companion! I would like to hear what he thinks of the world. The old tales cannot answer for him.',
 'Hello again, Corin. I am glad our first conversation was not the last.',
 t('Why does handmade pottery look uneven?', 'Sometimes because the maker chose it, sometimes because the maker is learning, and sometimes because the kiln had the last word.',
 ['Can you tell which?', 'Usually, if I know the work. I try not to invent a noble explanation for every wobble.'],
 ['Do you like perfect shapes?', 'Some. I also like a cup you can recognise without seeing its colour.'],
 ['What matters most in a cup?', 'That it holds the drink and feels pleasant to use. Art should remember where the tea goes.']),
 t('Do you enjoy teaching?', 'Yes, until someone tells me they have no talent after their first attempt. Nobody expects their first loaf to feed a wedding.',
 ['What do you tell them?', 'Make another. Notice one thing, change one thing, and give yourself time to learn.'],
 ['Were you naturally good at it?', 'No. I was naturally interested, which proved much more useful.'],
 ['What if they just want a pleasant afternoon?', 'Then that is a perfectly good result. Not every hobby needs a master at the end of it.']),
 t('Would you make a bowl for Aurelius?', 'If he wanted one. I would need to know what was comfortable for him instead of enlarging a bowl I liked.',
 ['He would appreciate the thought.', 'Then ask him what he actually prefers. I would enjoy the challenge.'],
 ['Would it fit in a kiln?', 'That is the next question. Enthusiasm must eventually speak to the measurements.'],
 ['We could hardly carry it everywhere.', 'True. Perhaps it would be something for a place you came home to.']),
 t('Do people value your work?', 'Some treasure a cup for years. Others break it and ask why I cannot make an exact replacement from memory.',
 ['Can you make a close match?', 'Close, yes. I explain the difference before promising more.'],
 ['Does breaking one upset you?', 'A little. But a cup that gets used has done more than one kept forever in a box.'],
 ['I would be afraid to use a precious gift.', 'Let the giver tell you what they hoped for. They may prefer seeing it at breakfast.']),
 t('What would you make to remember this year?', 'A set of bowls for friends. Something that makes us meet again, instead of a monument we walk past.',
 ['Would you decorate them alike?', 'Enough to belong together, not enough to lose each person’s favourite.'],
 ['Would you put dragons on them?', 'Only if that is what my friends wanted. I have learned to ask the people who will use the bowls.'],
 ['That sounds like a good celebration.', 'Then I shall put the idea into clay before I improve it beyond recognition.']));

p('Ivo','Young draughtsman','Ivo sketches imaginary machines and is beginning to appreciate the ordinary skills needed to make an idea useful.',
 ['I’m Ivo. I know I should say hello first, but is your dragon really travelling with you?', 'Hello first is easy enough. I’m Corin, he is Aurelius, and yes, we travel together.'],
 'I’m Ivo. Do you mind questions? I can usually stop after three, if warned.',
 'You travel with a dragon! I have been drawing flying machines without ever seeing how a real flying creature that large moves.',
 'Corin! I have narrowed today’s questions down considerably.',
 t('What do you like drawing?', 'Machines that solve one problem while probably creating several I have not drawn yet.',
 ['What was the latest?', 'A device to carry laundry upstairs. My mother suggested carrying the basket before building a tower in the house.'],
 ['Do any of them work?', 'Small ones. The large ones are still enjoying the freedom of being drawings.'],
 ['I like that you keep trying.', 'Thank you. I am learning to try something small enough to finish.']),
 t('Who helps you learn?', 'Anyone willing to explain their work. I used to ask only about the impressive part and miss what made it possible.',
 ['What do you ask now?', 'What usually goes wrong. People become wonderfully specific.'],
 ['Do they have time for you?', 'Some do. I am getting better at asking whether it is a good moment.'],
 ['Have you visited the smithy?', 'Yes. Dunstan made me draw the tool accurately before improving it. A deeply inconvenient lesson.']),
 t('Would you like to ask Aurelius something?', 'Yes. Does he have to think about every wingbeat, or does flying feel as ordinary as walking?',
 ['I can ask him that.', 'Thank you. I am more interested in his answer than in making my sketch look clever.'],
 ['I would like to know too.', 'Then it is a worthwhile question even if neither of us can put the answer into a machine.'],
 ['He might prefer a break from questions.', 'Of course. Curiosity is mine to manage, not his job to satisfy.']),
 t('Do you ever get discouraged?', 'Usually when something looks simple after another person has finished it. I forget I am only seeing the successful attempt.',
 ['I do that with sword practice.', 'Then perhaps we should compare mistakes sometime. It would be a reassuringly long conversation.'],
 ['What helps you continue?', 'Finding one part that is better than last time. A small improvement is still real.'],
 ['You could ask about their first attempt.', 'I have started doing that. The answers are much more encouraging than praise.']),
 t('Have you finished a small invention?', 'A stand that keeps a book open while I draw. Nothing flies, turns itself, or threatens the stairs.',
 ['Do you use it?', 'Every day. I am trying to accept that as a more useful achievement than looking impressive.'],
 ['Will you make another?', 'A friend asked for one. It feels rather good to have a reason besides proving I could.'],
 ['Could you improve it?', 'Certainly. But first I am enjoying the astonishing fact that it works.']));

p('Merrin','Keen local walker','Merrin knows Forgewick’s everyday paths and finds more pleasure in noticing a familiar place than collecting distant destinations.',
 ['I’m Merrin. I was going to ask which road brought you here, but I see you may have a rather different view of roads.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius. We still use them, though flying has changed how the world looks.'],
 'Merrin. Are you exploring Forgewick, or heading somewhere in particular?',
 'You travel with a dragon? Then you can tell me whether a place looks entirely different from above. I have often wondered.',
 'Hello again, Corin. Have you had a chance to look around?',
 t('Do you enjoy walking the same paths?', 'Yes. Familiarity gives you room to notice small changes instead of spending the whole walk working out where you are.',
 ['What sort of changes?', 'A new gate, a repaired step, someone who has begun taking their rest outdoors. A town is never quite finished.'],
 ['Do you ever get bored?', 'Certainly. Then I take a different turning. I do not consider it a failure of loyalty.'],
 ['I used to know Millwood that way.', 'You may find it pleasantly strange when you return. Both you and the place will have changed a little.']),
 t('Can you tell when someone is lost?', 'Often. They walk confidently past the same place twice, hoping the place will be embarrassed into helping them.',
 ['That sounds like me.', 'It sounds like almost everyone. Asking saves a great deal of determined walking.'],
 ['Do you offer help?', 'I ask whether they want directions. Nobody enjoys being seized by a helpful stranger.'],
 ['Have you ever given the wrong directions?', 'Once. I went after the traveller when I realised. I was very glad they walked slowly.']),
 t('What would you ask Aurelius about flying?', 'Whether he likes looking down or looking ahead. People describe the view, but rarely the feeling of having somewhere to go.',
 ['He enjoys having room to move.', 'I can understand that. Some walks are for reaching a place; others are for stretching yourself.'],
 ['Sometimes we simply look around.', 'Then I am glad the journey leaves room for that.'],
 ['I can ask him when he wants to talk.', 'Thank you. There is no deadline on my curiosity.']),
 t('What makes somewhere feel like home?', 'Knowing a small useful thing nobody thought to write down. Which neighbour welcomes a knock, for instance.',
 ['I thought it was knowing the streets.', 'That helps you reach the houses. People make you glad you reached them.'],
 ['Can a traveller feel at home?', 'For a little while, certainly. You need not promise to stay forever before accepting a welcome.'],
 ['I miss that feeling.', 'Then let this be a familiar door when you pass through Forgewick again.']),
 t('Would you like to hear about somewhere new?', 'Very much. Tell me about the part you noticed before you knew what you were supposed to admire.',
 ['You do not want the grand story?', 'I enjoy those too. But your own first impression tells me something a guide would leave out.'],
 ['I notice the people first, lately.', 'That sounds like a good habit to bring home.'],
 ['I will keep something in mind for next time.', 'Then I have another visit to look forward to.']));

p('Dunstan','Blacksmith','Dunstan is a direct, generous craftsman. His brother Sela works glass in Sandspire, and their different trades give them plenty to argue about.',
 ['A dragon at my workshop. I’m Dunstan. Tell me you have both come through the road in one piece.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius. We have, but I would be grateful for someone who understands equipment better than I do.', 'Then you have come to a useful place. We can discuss what you need.'],
 'Dunstan. What can I help you with, traveller?',
 'A dragon travels with you? Then you have an unusual friend and the same need as any traveller to come home safely. I can help with the equipment.',
 ()=>smithUpgrade?'Corin. Good to see you. How is the equipment holding up?':'Corin. Good to see you. What would you like to ask?',
 t('How did you choose this trade?', 'I repaired a handle as a boy and watched my mother use it every day. Making something useful felt better than being praised for being clever.',
 ['Did you always enjoy the work?', 'No. Some days a stubborn piece of metal was simply a stubborn piece of metal.'],
 ['Who taught you?', 'A patient smith who made me finish the ordinary jobs properly. I understood the patience much later.'],
 ['What do you most like making?', 'Whatever somebody needs enough to stop struggling when they receive it.']),
 t('Does your family live in Forgewick?', 'My brother Sela works glass in Sandspire. We get along very well, provided neither of us is asked whose work is more delicate.',
 ['Do you miss having him nearby?', 'Yes. I tell him by asking when he intends to visit and stop sending messages.'],
 ['Why did he move to Sandspire?', 'Good sand for his glass, and the caravan trade. He wanted to find out what he could make of the opportunity.'],
 ['Are your arguments serious?', 'Sometimes. We still make sure the other has what he needs.']),
 t('Would you work with dragon fire?', 'I would ask what Aurelius wanted from the arrangement first. I have enough fuel; I do not need to turn a guest into part of the workshop.',
 ['He might be curious about your work.', 'Then I would show him. Curiosity is a better beginning than expecting a favour.'],
 ['Could his fire make different metal?', 'I would need careful trials before claiming anything. A marvellous source of heat does not excuse guessing.'],
 ['I am glad you think of him as a guest.', 'What else should he be? He came with a friend, not a work order.']),
 t('What should I remember about good equipment?', 'It helps you survive mistakes. It does not make every risk a sensible one.',
 ['So I should still avoid attacks.', 'Yes. Give the armour fewer chances to prove its value.'],
 ['How do I know when I need help?', 'Ask before damage becomes failure. Pride is an expensive reason to keep a problem to yourself.'],
 ['I am still learning to use the sword.', 'Then practise with attention. A better blade deserves a careful hand.']),
 t('Why did you help us?', 'Because you needed help, and I could provide it. I did not require you to become important first.',
 ['I would like to repay you.', 'Remember who helped you when somebody else needs the same chance. That is enough for me.'],
 ['It made a difference.', 'I am pleased. A craftsman likes to hear his work was useful.'],
 ['I will try to bring it all home safely.', 'Bring yourself and your friend. The equipment comes after that.']));

p('Alderic','Keeper of the Lightning sanctuary','Alderic preserves the riders’ knowledge in Forgewick’s temple and treats inheritance as a responsibility to teach rather than a right to command.',
 ['A living dragon, here in the sanctuary. I am Alderic, its keeper. May I ask who has brought him this far?', 'I’m Corin. His name is Aurelius. We would like to understand the Heartstones better.', 'Then let us speak plainly about what you have come to find.'],
 'I am Alderic, keeper of this sanctuary. What has brought you through the temple?',
 'You have come on behalf of a dragon companion. Then I will explain what this sanctuary preserves, without pretending he is here to hear it.',
 'Welcome back, Corin. What would you like to understand more clearly?',
 t('What does the Lightning Heartstone do?', ()=>breathHas.lightning?'You have claimed Lightning. Aurelius can now use that breath attack; the stone does not need to occupy one of your charm slots.':'The sanctuary’s reward chest holds the Lightning Heartstone. Claim it to unlock Aurelius’s Lightning breath; reaching this room alone does not grant it.',
 ['How do we use it?', 'Open the Dragon menu in battle and choose Lightning once it has been unlocked. The other breath attacks remain available.'],
 ['Is this the only Heartstone we need?', 'No. Sandspire’s temple preserves Ice, and the temple near Hollybeck preserves Shadow. Each must be claimed.'],
 ['Does having it mean we understand it?', 'It gives Aurelius the attack. Learning when to use it is something the two of you do together.']),
 t('Why are the Heartstones kept separately?', 'Their powers were entrusted to different sanctuaries. A single ruler should not be able to take an entire inheritance simply by seizing one room.',
 ['Did the arrangement keep them safe?', 'For a time. No arrangement remains wise merely because it is old.'],
 ['Is gathering them dangerous?', 'Power can be misused, but leaving it divided has not made the world safe either. What you choose to do matters.'],
 ['Why let us claim them?', 'You have reached this sanctuary with your companion. My task is to explain the inheritance, not invent another owner for it.']),
 t('Should a rider command a dragon?', 'You will need to act together in danger. That does not make every decision in the friendship the rider’s to take.',
 ['Aurelius and I can speak mind to mind.', 'Then use that gift to listen as carefully as you speak. Understanding a sentence is not always understanding a wish.'],
 ['What if we disagree during a fight?', 'Prepare together when you are safe. Do not leave every question until you have no time to discuss it.'],
 ['I do not want to become his master.', 'Then remember that intention in the ordinary decisions as well as the grand ones.']),
 t('What has the temple failed to preserve?', 'The names of many ordinary people who kept the riders alive: cooks, healers, stable hands, friends. A record of great deeds can become strangely lonely.',
 ['Could those names be recovered?', 'Some. I would rather admit the gaps than fill them with impressive inventions.'],
 ['Why were they left out?', 'People recording power often look past the work that supports it. We should learn from that mistake.'],
 ['We have had help from so many people.', 'Then remember them as people, not merely as steps on your road.']),
 t('What should we carry away from the temple?', 'The knowledge that an inheritance can be changed by the person receiving it. You need not repeat every choice the old riders made.',
 ['Even the choices people celebrate?', 'Especially examine those. Admiration can make a poor habit difficult to recognise.'],
 ['What if we make our own mistakes?', 'Then learn, repair what you can, and let someone else question you. That is more useful than claiming certainty.'],
 ['We want a life beyond fighting.', 'Hold on to that. A power worth using ought to leave room for the life it protects.']));

p('Miner Marn','Road crew leader','Marn is an experienced miner who takes responsibility for the crew without pretending that experience makes anyone infallible.',
 ['Easy a moment. A dragon is a new visitor for this crew. I’m Marn; are the two of you travelling together?', 'Corin, and Aurelius. We are. Let us know where you need space and we will keep clear.'],
 'Marn. If you want to know about the east road, ask before trying to squeeze past anything.',
 'A dragon companion. Then I am glad you stopped to ask about the road instead of assuming wings settle every problem.',
 'Corin. Have you come to ask about the road, or give us a more interesting subject?',
 t('Can we take the road towards Sandspire?', ()=>JOURNEY_GATES.forgewick.open()?'The east road is clear. You can continue towards Sandspire; leave room for any carts using the passage.':'We are still clearing the east road. '+(!smithUpgrade||!charm.edge?'Dunstan can help you finish collecting your equipment while we work. '+(!breathHas.lightning?'There is also the Lightning Heartstone to claim in Forgewick Temple.':'You have already claimed Lightning, so the smithy is your remaining stop.'):'You have Dunstan’s equipment. Use the delay to claim the Lightning Heartstone in Forgewick Temple; we expect the passage to be ready by your return.'),
 ['Where should we go first?', ()=>!smithUpgrade||!charm.edge?'Speak to Dunstan at his smithy and finish collecting the equipment he offers. Then make sure you have claimed the Lightning Heartstone in the temple.':!breathHas.lightning?'You have Dunstan’s equipment. Explore Forgewick Temple and claim the Lightning Heartstone from its reward chest.':'You have done the preparation. The east road is open when you want to continue.'],
 ['Is there another task you need us to do?', 'No. You do not need to collect stones or move carts for us. The crew is handling the repair.'],
 ['Can we return to the town?', 'Yes. This work concerns the eastward passage; it is not a reason to stop you returning to Forgewick.']),
 t('What makes a good crew leader?', 'Knowing which questions belong to the person who can actually see the problem. My apprentice Nerik deserves to be heard, even when I have already formed an opinion.',
 ['Does that mean listening to Nerik?', 'Certainly. He may be newer, but he has his own pair of eyes.'],
 ['What if someone questions your order?', 'I want to hear the concern. A safe shift matters more than my sounding certain.'],
 ['Have you ever been wrong?', 'Often enough to appreciate being told before the mistake became expensive.']),
 t('Could Aurelius clear the road?', 'I would not ask a visitor to pull at a load we have not finished making safe. Strength does not tell you what will shift next.',
 ['We will leave the repair to you.', 'Thank you. Giving workers room can be useful help.'],
 ['He would not want anyone hurt.', 'Then we agree about the important part.'],
 ['I thought it might save time.', 'A reasonable thought. I would still rather take the time than risk the crew on a guess.']),
 t('What do you do after a shift?', 'Wash, eat, and try to stop explaining work to people who have politely asked about something else.',
 ['What else do you enjoy?', 'Growing herbs badly and accusing the weather. Nerik finds it very entertaining.'],
 ['Do you spend time with the crew?', 'Sometimes. We also deserve to meet people who have never heard our work arguments.'],
 ['Do you manage to switch off?', 'Better when I know everyone got home. That is the part I want to keep remembering.']),
 t('What do you hope Nerik learns from you?', 'To become good enough that he can disagree with me for a well-explained reason. I have no ambition to train an echo.',
 ['That is an unusual answer.', 'Only if you think teaching means remaining the cleverest person in the conversation.'],
 ['Has he managed it yet?', 'Several times. I am pleased, after an appropriate moment of irritation.'],
 ['Would you tell him that?', 'Yes. A learner should not have to guess whether you trust him.']));

p('Miner Nerik','Young road worker','Nerik is learning a demanding trade and discovering that asking a clear question is more useful than pretending to know.',
 ['Marn said we might have travellers, but he left out the dragon. I’m Nerik. Are you both all right there?', 'I’m Corin, and this is Aurelius. We are fine. We will wait if you need us to keep back.'],
 'Nerik. Marn can answer the complicated questions; I can answer more of them than I used to.',
 'You travel with a dragon? I have been trying not to look surprised by anything at work. That would defeat the attempt completely.',
 'Hello, Corin. How is your share of the learning going?',
 t('How is the road work going?', ()=>JOURNEY_GATES.forgewick.open()?'Finished and checked. The road towards Sandspire is open now. I am rather proud of a repair people can pass without noticing.':'The east passage is still being cleared. '+(!smithUpgrade||!charm.edge?'Check with Dunstan and finish collecting his equipment. '+(!breathHas.lightning?'You can also claim the Lightning Heartstone in the temple before continuing.':'You have already collected Lightning.'):'Your equipment is ready. Claim the Lightning Heartstone in the temple while the crew finishes here.'),
 ['Does the repair need anything from me?', 'No materials, no payment. Keep clear of the crew while we finish.'],
 ['What should I check before heading east?', ()=>!smithUpgrade||!charm.edge?'Make sure you have collected Dunstan’s sword-and-armour upgrade and Whetstone, as well as the Lightning Heartstone.':!breathHas.lightning?'Claim the Lightning Heartstone from the temple chest. Getting to the sanctuary without opening the reward is not the same thing.':'You have collected the equipment and Lightning. You can take the open road.'],
 ['Is Marn satisfied with your work?', 'He checks it carefully. I would rather know it is sound than hear a quick compliment.']),
 t('What was hardest when you began?', 'Saying I did not understand. I wasted more time trying to look capable than a simple question would have taken.',
 ['I know that feeling.', 'It is reassuring that someone travelling with a dragon still knows it.'],
 ['What changed?', 'Marn asked me to explain an instruction back to him. He made checking ordinary instead of embarrassing.'],
 ['Do you ask more now?', 'Yes. The questions are getting better, which is a kind of progress.']),
 t('What would you ask a dragon?', 'Whether he ever feels new at something. People speak about dragons as if knowing how to fly means knowing everything.',
 ['He is learning about this world too.', 'Then I hope he finds people willing to explain it without talking down to him.'],
 ['I can ask him later.', 'Thank you. I would enjoy hearing his answer when he wants to give it.'],
 ['We have both made mistakes.', 'That is more encouraging than a perfect heroic account would have been.']),
 t('Do you want to keep doing this work?', 'For now. I like seeing something become safer because we worked on it. I am less certain about enjoying the early mornings.',
 ['Does the satisfaction make up for them?', 'Usually by afternoon. Never when I first wake up.'],
 ['Would you like to lead a crew?', 'Eventually, perhaps. I want to learn the work before learning to sound important.'],
 ['You could change your mind later.', 'I remind myself of that. Choosing a trade need not mean writing the rest of my life in stone.']),
 t('Do you feel more at home in the crew?', 'Yes. I have stopped waiting for someone to discover I am still learning. They all know; that is why they teach me.',
 ['That must be a relief.', 'It is. I can use the effort on the work instead of looking untroubled.'],
 ['What are you proud of?', 'Catching a small mistake before it became anyone else’s problem. Quiet progress, but mine.'],
 ['Marn seems to trust you.', 'I think he does. Hearing it from somebody else makes me rather pleased.']));

p('Brother Edrin','Keeper of Forgewick’s chapel','Edrin keeps a congregation together under Halvard’s ban on dragon worship. His brother Cael maintains a hidden church in the desert.',
 ['A living dragon in our chapel. I am Brother Edrin. Forgive me; this is something I have hoped for without knowing what I would say.', 'I’m Corin. This is Aurelius. We would like to understand this place, if you have time.', 'You are both welcome. You need not share our beliefs to ask about them.'],
 'I am Brother Edrin. Welcome to the chapel. Is there something you would like to ask?',
 'You are travelling with a dragon. That is remarkable news for this congregation. I would like to meet him, but I will not ask you to bring him here simply to fulfil our hopes.',
 'Welcome back, Corin. What would you like to talk about today?',
 t('Why is the chapel so plain?', ()=>wonAll?'Halvard’s soldiers made us remove the dragon window and statues. His defeat means we can decide what to restore, but the work is still ahead of us.':'Halvard forbids gatherings for dragon worship. His soldiers made us remove the dragon window and statues; keeping the room bare is one condition under which we have been allowed to remain.',
 ['Why keep gathering here?', 'People need one another, especially when they are frightened. The room can still give us that.'],
 ['Does everyone here worship dragons?', 'No. Some come for company, or to sit somewhere familiar. Belief is not a fee at the door.'],
 ['How do you decide what to do next?', 'By speaking with the people who use this place. They have borne the consequences of decisions made without them.']),
 t('What does dragon worship mean to you?', 'Gratitude, wonder, and a duty to care for the living world. It should not mean demanding that a living dragon act out every story we have told.',
 ['I do not think of Aurelius as a god.', 'You need not. You know him as a companion. I would be foolish to dismiss that knowledge.'],
 ['What if he does not want to be worshipped?', 'Then we must listen. Reverence that refuses to hear its subject has become something selfish.'],
 ['Why do the old stories matter?', 'They shape how people imagine courage and kindness. That makes it important to question the cruel ones.']),
 t('Will you expect anything from Aurelius?', 'Good manners, as I would from any guest. No miracle, performance, or promise to solve our difficulties.',
 ['He might be relieved to hear that.', 'Then please tell him plainly. A welcome with hidden conditions is not much of a welcome.'],
 ['Can we leave whenever we need to?', 'Of course. Staying longer does not make you more worthy of our kindness.'],
 ['What if people crowd around him?', 'I will ask them to give him room. Their joy does not cancel his comfort.']),
 t('Have you always been certain of your faith?', 'No. I have continued to care for people on days when I was uncertain about nearly everything else.',
 ['Do you tell the congregation that?', 'When it is useful. They should not mistake a calm voice for a life without questions.'],
 ['What keeps you here?', 'The people who return, and the ones who need a welcome for the first time.'],
 ['Can someone disagree with you here?', 'Yes. I hope the disagreement leaves us understanding one another more clearly.']),
 t('What would you like this chapel to become?', 'A place where nobody has to rehearse a safe answer before coming through the door.',
 ['Would you restore the dragon art?', 'Yes, with the congregation’s help. I would like beauty to return without making belonging depend on admiring it.'],
 ['Could Aurelius help choose it?', 'If he wanted to. His opinion would be welcome, not an obligation.'],
 ['I hope we can visit in quieter times.', 'So do I. You will not need to arrive with extraordinary news.']));

p('Brother Oswin','Chapel caretaker','Oswin keeps the chapel usable and likes the ordinary tasks that make a welcome real.',
 ['A dragon in the aisle. I am Brother Oswin, and I have suddenly forgotten every grand welcome I imagined.', 'I’m Corin, and he is Aurelius. An ordinary hello will suit us both.', 'Then hello. I can manage that rather well.'],
 'Brother Oswin. Welcome. Have you come to speak with Edrin, or simply to visit?',
 'A dragon companion. Edrin will be interested, though you are welcome here without bringing extraordinary news.',
 'Hello again, Corin. I am glad you found your way back.',
 t('What do you look after here?', 'Whatever makes the next person’s visit easier. A clean room is less impressive than a sermon, but people notice when neither is any good.',
 ['Do you enjoy the work?', 'Most of it. I have yet to develop a spiritual affection for sweeping.'],
 ['Does anyone help?', 'Yes. Asking clearly works better than sighing until someone notices.'],
 ['Do people thank you?', 'Often enough. I also like seeing someone settle comfortably without knowing why they can.']),
 t('Did you plan to join a chapel?', 'No. I came to help repair a door, stayed for a meal, and discovered I liked the company.',
 ['Did the door get repaired?', 'Eventually. I would prefer that detail not become the moral of the story.'],
 ['What made you stay?', 'Being useful without needing to be impressive.'],
 ['Did your family understand?', 'After I explained it. They had imagined something much more solemn than most of my days.']),
 t('Does meeting a dragon change your faith?', 'It changes my manners first. A living guest deserves more attention than the perfect creature I imagined.',
 ['Aurelius will appreciate that.', 'I hope so. I would like him to remember being comfortable here.'],
 ['Are you disappointed by ordinary dragon things?', 'Certainly not. Hunger and curiosity make him easier to welcome, not less wonderful.'],
 ['I do not share all the chapel’s beliefs.', 'Then we can still share a conversation.']),
 t('What do you find difficult about chapel life?', 'People sometimes apologise for ordinary feelings because they think a sacred place should make them instantly serene.',
 ['What do you tell them?', 'That they may sit down exactly as they are.'],
 ['Does that happen to you?', 'Yes. Usually when somebody has moved the broom and I am trying to appear charitable.'],
 ['Can a small joke help?', 'Frequently. Solemnity and kindness are not the same thing.']),
 t('What would make a good return visit?', 'You coming because you wanted to, with no duty to deliver us an inspiring tale.',
 ['We might have a very ordinary story.', 'Excellent. Ordinary stories are often easier to live in.'],
 ['Would Aurelius still cause a stir?', 'Probably. We can improve our welcome while remaining delighted to see him.'],
 ['Then we will stop when we can.', 'I shall be pleased, whenever that is.']));

p('Brother Ansel','Chapel singer','Ansel loves singing with other people and is learning to make room for imperfect voices, including his own.',
 ['I am Brother Ansel. I had songs prepared for the return of dragons. Seeing one makes me think listening should come first.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. We would enjoy hearing about the songs, once we have said hello.'],
 'Brother Ansel. You are welcome to listen, speak, or sit quietly here.',
 'You travel with a dragon? Then I hope the songs have left room for the person behind the legend.',
 'Welcome back, Corin. I have a question if you have a moment.',
 t('Does everybody have to sing?', 'No. A congregation is not an audition. Listening is a perfectly good way to be present.',
 ['I am not sure I sing well.', 'Most people judge themselves while imagining somebody else’s best performance.'],
 ['Do you teach anyone who asks?', 'Yes. We begin with breathing, which is less intimidating than beginning with beauty.'],
 ['Would humming be all right?', 'Very much so. A tune can welcome a small beginning.']),
 t('Have you ever ruined a song?', 'I began a verse too high and spent the rest of it discovering the limits of optimism.',
 ['Did anyone laugh?', 'Yes, including me once I could breathe.'],
 ['What did you do next?', 'Started again in a sensible key. An error need not become the entire service.'],
 ['Do you still get nervous?', 'Sometimes. Knowing the feeling makes me gentler with other singers.']),
 t('Would you sing for Aurelius?', 'If he wanted to listen. I would not make him endure a ceremony because I had dreamed of performing one.',
 ['I can ask what he likes.', 'Thank you. I would welcome an honest preference.'],
 ['Maybe something gentle.', 'A good place to begin. Wonder does not require maximum volume.'],
 ['Would it bother you if he left?', 'Only if we had made him too uncomfortable to tell us he wanted to.']),
 t('Why keep old songs?', 'A melody can carry the memory of people who no longer have anyone to tell their stories.',
 ['Do the words ever change?', 'Yes. Keeping something alive is different from insisting it must never move.'],
 ['How do you know which version is right?', 'I explain what I know and admit what I do not. A lovely song does not need a false pedigree.'],
 ['Can a new song matter as much?', 'Certainly. Someone has to begin what another person will inherit.']),
 t('What song would suit a homecoming?', 'One the people arriving recognise. I would rather hear them join in than admire my clever choice.',
 ['I would choose something Nan knows.', 'Then it would bring more than one part of home into the room.'],
 ['Aurelius would need a new tradition.', 'Or one the two of you begin together.'],
 ['Perhaps no song at first. Just a rest.', 'Then the music can wait. That is a good thing for a singer to remember.']));

p('Mara Bell','Chapel neighbour','Mara enjoys family stories, worries about losing their details, and has little patience for being called timid.',
 ['I’m Mara Bell. I have imagined seeing a dragon since childhood. I did not expect to feel shy about saying hello.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius. We can start with hello and leave the grand part for another day.'],
 'Mara Bell. Have you come to meet someone here?',
 'A dragon travels with you? I would like to hear about him as he is, not only how the old tales taught me to imagine him.',
 'Corin, hello. It is pleasant to recognise a visitor.',
 t('Who told you the old dragon stories?', 'My aunt. She gave minor characters so much attention that we sometimes forgot which adventure she had begun.',
 ['Did you mind?', 'Not at all. I wanted to know whether the cook got home safely as much as the rider.'],
 ['Do you remember the stories clearly?', 'Pieces. I ask relatives before calling my memory the only correct version.'],
 ['Did she believe them?', 'Some, I think. Mostly she believed children deserved an interesting evening.']),
 t('What do you wish you had asked your family?', 'Why they chose things. I remember what they did, but I would like to understand more of what they hoped for.',
 ['Can anyone still tell you?', 'Some people can. I am trying to ask while the answers are still there to hear.'],
 ['Nan has stories I have not heard yet.', 'Then leave time for them when you can. You do not have to ask everything in one visit.'],
 ['Would you write them down?', 'I have begun. Even a plain sentence can keep a detail from disappearing.']),
 t('Does Aurelius resemble the dragons in those stories?', 'In the broad outline, perhaps. I am more interested in where the stories got him wrong.',
 ['He is not a creature from somebody else’s tale.', 'Exactly. I would like to meet him without forcing a childhood picture over him.'],
 ['Some of the old memories matter to him too.', 'Then I hope he gets to choose which ones he shares.'],
 ['You can ask us questions.', 'Thank you. I shall try to ask questions with room for a surprising answer.']),
 t('Were you frightened when the soldiers came?', 'Yes. I dislike the idea that admitting fear erases everything somebody did despite it.',
 ['What did you do?', 'Helped a neighbour get home. It was ordinary and it mattered to her.'],
 ['You do not need to prove anything to me.', 'Thank you. I would rather be understood than congratulated inaccurately.'],
 ['I get frightened too.', 'I believe you. It makes your choices more human, not less worthwhile.']),
 t('What would you like people to remember of this time?', 'The people who kept visiting one another. Fear tries to make a town into separate locked rooms.',
 ['Did the chapel help?', 'For many of us. Other people found company elsewhere, and that mattered too.'],
 ['Would you tell that story yourself?', 'I am trying. It deserves more than being the quiet part of somebody else’s account.'],
 ['I am glad we met.', 'So am I, Corin. You may put that detail in your own account.']));

p('Teren Vale','Wagon repairer','Teren attends the chapel with more questions than certainty and believes good company can survive both.',
 ['A dragon. I’m Teren Vale, and I have just lost an argument I have been having with myself for years.', 'I’m Corin. This is Aurelius. Which part of the argument?', 'Whether I would know what to say if I ever met one. Apparently not.'],
 'Teren Vale. I come here for company as much as anything. What brings you?',
 'You travel with a dragon? That gives me questions rather than answers, but I am pleased to have better questions.',
 'Corin, good to see you. Have you room for a question or two?',
 t('Do you share Edrin’s beliefs?', 'Some. He knows which parts I question and has not attempted to settle them by asking me to leave.',
 ['Does that surprise you?', 'It did at first. I had grown used to disagreement being treated as discourtesy.'],
 ['What keeps you coming?', 'The company and the possibility of a conversation I did not expect.'],
 ['I have questions too.', 'Then we shall not run out of subjects.']),
 t('What do you repair?', 'Wagons, when someone admits that the noise is a problem before a wheel makes the argument for me.',
 ['Do people wait too long?', 'Frequently. Hope is a poor lubricant.'],
 ['Is the work satisfying?', 'Very, when a cart leaves quietly and the owner stops flinching at every bump.'],
 ['Do you enjoy travelling in them?', 'More when someone else is responsible for listening to the axle.']),
 t('Does seeing Aurelius settle your questions?', 'It settles whether this particular dragon exists. What his existence means is something I should be careful about deciding for him.',
 ['I appreciate that distinction.', 'So would I, if people kept assigning meaning to my arrival.'],
 ['You are allowed to be amazed.', 'Oh, I am. Amazement and a little careful thinking can share the same head.'],
 ['What would you like to know about him?', 'What he enjoys when nobody is asking him to be extraordinary.']),
 t('Are you good at changing your mind?', 'Better after I have eaten. Before that I can defend a foolish position with remarkable energy.',
 ['A practical weakness to recognise.', 'I recommend it. Some arguments need evidence; others need lunch.'],
 ['Do you apologise afterwards?', 'When I have been unpleasant. Being hungry is an explanation, not a pardon.'],
 ['Does Edrin know that?', 'He has quietly suggested a meal more than once.']),
 t('What would make you feel hopeful?', 'People asking what can be repaired instead of insisting everything must return to exactly how they remember it.',
 ['Does that apply to more than wagons?', 'Occasionally I permit myself a thought outside my trade.'],
 ['What would you keep?', 'The people, where I can. Familiarity need not mean keeping every bad arrangement.'],
 ['I want something better after all this.', 'Then keep asking what better would look like in an ordinary day.']));

p('Nessa Flint','Older sister and chapel visitor','Nessa Flint is practical, playful, and determined to answer her younger brother’s questions without inventing certainty.',
 ['I’m Nessa Flint. My little brother keeps asking whether dragons are real. I have a much better answer now.', 'I’m Corin. This is Aurelius. You can tell him you met a dragon, but please leave room for us being ordinary people too.'],
 'Nessa Flint. Have you come for the service, or to meet someone?',
 'You travel with a dragon? My brother will want a hundred questions answered. I will remind him you have a journey, not an appointment as his tutor.',
 'Hello, Corin. I have tried to keep my family’s questions to a manageable number.',
 t('What does your brother ask you?', 'Everything. Why people argue, where rain begins, whether a beetle knows it is upside down. I run out of answers long before he runs out of interest.',
 ['Do you tell him when you do not know?', 'Yes. He was astonished at first and has since begun keeping a list.'],
 ['Does he ask anyone else?', 'Anyone within reach. You have been warned.'],
 ['I was rather like that.', 'Then I hope somebody answered you kindly.']),
 t('What games do you play together?', 'Treasure hunts. He has started hiding the clues himself, which makes them much harder for either of us to find.',
 ['Does he remember where he put them?', 'With unjustified confidence.'],
 ['What counts as treasure?', 'Something small and a reason to be pleased. The hunt is most of the gift.'],
 ['Would a dragon make the game too easy?', 'Only if we made the clues about things people can see from the sky.']),
 t('What will you tell him about Aurelius?', 'That he travels with a friend and deserves to be asked before anyone touches him. Wonder can learn manners.',
 ['Thank you. That would help.', 'Then that is where the story will begin.'],
 ['Tell him Aurelius has his own opinions.', 'Gladly. That should improve the questions.'],
 ['Would he be frightened?', 'Possibly. I would let him be curious from a distance until he felt ready.']),
 t('Why do you come to the chapel?', 'Sometimes for the service. Sometimes because adults are allowed to need a calm hour too.',
 ['Do you get much time to yourself?', 'Enough if I remember to ask for it. Everyone assumes I will say when I need help.'],
 ['Do you bring your brother?', 'Sometimes. He is learning that a quiet place is still allowed to contain a child.'],
 ['Would you rather I let you rest?', 'I am happy to talk. Thank you for checking.']),
 t('What answer would you like to give him about the future?', 'An honest one with something to look forward to. I cannot promise him a world without trouble.',
 ['What can you promise?', 'That he can ask me questions, and I will keep trying to help him understand.'],
 ['Children notice when adults are worried.', 'Yes. Pretending they notice nothing leaves them guessing alone.'],
 ['I hope we help make that future kinder.', 'So do I. You need not carry the whole responsibility yourselves.']));

p('Orris Reed','Millwright','Orris likes quiet rooms, clear explanations, and the company of people who do not mistake a reserved manner for dislike.',
 ['I’m Orris Reed. The dragon startled me, but I would rather say that plainly than make you wonder why I went quiet.', 'Corin. His name is Aurelius. We can give you room.', 'Thank you. I would still like to speak with you.'],
 'Orris Reed. Hello. I do not always have much to say at first, but you are welcome to talk.',
 'A dragon companion. I think I would need a moment to get used to meeting him. That is not a refusal of the introduction.',
 'Corin, hello. It is easier to begin when I recognise someone.',
 t('What does a millwright do?', 'Builds and repairs the machinery that turns a mill. A great many ordinary meals depend on work people only notice when it stops.',
 ['What do you enjoy about it?', 'Finding the small fault that explains the large problem.'],
 ['Is it noisy work?', 'Often. That is partly why I appreciate a quiet room afterwards.'],
 ['Do you like explaining it?', 'When somebody is interested, yes. I may take a moment to choose the beginning.']),
 t('Do you prefer listening?', 'Often. It gives me time to understand before I offer an opinion I will immediately have to repair.',
 ['People do not always give you time.', 'No. I am learning to say that I am thinking, rather than hoping they will guess.'],
 ['Does silence ever bother you?', 'Only when somebody treats it as proof we are failing to get along.'],
 ['We can take our time.', 'Thank you. That makes conversation considerably easier.']),
 t('Would meeting Aurelius help you feel less frightened?', 'Perhaps. I would like a calm introduction, not a test of whether I am brave enough to stand still.',
 ['That sounds fair.', 'I am glad. People often mean well when they hurry someone past a fear.'],
 ['He can keep his distance.', 'Then I can pay attention to him rather than the distance.'],
 ['You do not have to do it today.', 'Thank you. Having a choice makes the idea less daunting.']),
 t('What do you enjoy besides work?', 'Watching water. The kind of pastime people try to improve by adding a fishing rod and an objective.',
 ['You just watch it?', 'Yes. I am astonishingly accomplished at doing very little beside a river.'],
 ['I enjoy fishing.', 'Then you may fish while I watch. Neither of us needs to persuade the other.'],
 ['That sounds peaceful.', 'It usually is. I recommend remembering that peaceful things exist.']),
 t('Are you glad we spoke?', 'Yes. You let me be quiet without deciding I was unfriendly.',
 ['I am glad I gave the right impression.', 'You did. A small courtesy can make a conversation much better.'],
 ['I hope Aurelius feels welcome too.', 'Please tell him he is. I can be welcoming while still getting used to someone.'],
 ['We will say hello when we return.', 'I would like that, Corin.']));

p('Elva Moss','Gardener','Elva grows herbs and vegetables, enjoys firm opinions about soil, and regards hospitality as an ordinary responsibility.',
 ['I’m Elva Moss. A dragon in this room is a wonderful surprise. I hope nobody has made you both feel cornered.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. We are comfortable so far. Thank you for asking before adding to the fuss.'],
 'Elva Moss. Welcome. Have you had a chance to rest?',
 'A dragon companion? Then I hope people make room for him as well as discussing him. A welcome should have some practical effect.',
 'Corin, welcome back. How are you both?',
 t('What do you like growing?', 'Beans. They are generous when they are pleased and extremely clear when they are not.',
 ['How do you know they are pleased?', 'They grow. Gardeners sometimes bury the simple answer under impressive language.'],
 ['Do you grow flowers too?', 'Yes. A useful garden is allowed to give you pleasure as well as supper.'],
 ['I do not know much about gardening.', 'Neither did I before killing several unfortunate plants.']),
 t('Do you share what you grow?', 'When there is enough. I have learned to ask whether someone wants more beans before arriving with another basket.',
 ['Can there be too many beans?', 'There can certainly be too many surprise deliveries of them.'],
 ['What do you get in return?', 'Sometimes something useful, sometimes thanks. I try not to turn surplus vegetables into a debt.'],
 ['Does the whole street garden?', 'Enough people do that our mistakes become a useful local education.']),
 t('Would Aurelius be welcome in a garden?', 'With a little care. I would show him where the plants are instead of scolding him for not knowing.',
 ['His tail takes more room than he expects.', 'Then we would leave more room. Gardens are not improved by humiliating visitors.'],
 ['He might like watching things grow.', 'I would enjoy that company. Plants give a conversation somewhere comfortable to pause.'],
 ['Would you be worried about his fire?', 'I would ask about it plainly. Worry becomes less useful when nobody is allowed to discuss it.']),
 t('What keeps you coming here?', 'People. I can think about my beliefs in a garden, but a garden rarely tells me a neighbour needs company.',
 ['Do you know everyone?', 'Not yet. New people deserve a place before they become familiar.'],
 ['Would you welcome someone who disagreed?', 'Yes. I would ask them not to be cruel, which is what I ask of people who agree with me too.'],
 ['That sounds like a good beginning.', 'A beginning still needs practice. We do our best.']),
 t('What would you like us to remember?', 'That you are allowed to arrive hungry, tired, or without good news. Hospitality should not require an entertaining guest.',
 ['We have all three sorts of day.', 'Then I am glad you know a place to stop.'],
 ['Does that include Aurelius?', 'Of course. I have been listening when you say “we”.'],
 ['Thank you, Elva.', 'You are welcome, Corin. No grander answer is needed.']));

p('Brennor Ash','Foundry worker','Brennor speaks cautiously in groups and is discovering that a measured opinion can still be a strong one.',
 ['Brennor Ash. I ought to say something wise about meeting a dragon, but mostly I am glad he has arrived with a friend.', 'I’m Corin. His name is Aurelius. We are glad to find people willing to meet us.'],
 'Brennor Ash. Hello. I have a little time if you would like to talk.',
 'A dragon companion. I hope people give you both a chance to speak for yourselves. They are quick to decide what something means.',
 'Corin, hello. I have become less surprised by the idea of you returning, which is rather pleasant.',
 t('Do you find it difficult to speak in a group?', 'I usually think of a useful contribution after everyone has decided what they intend to do.',
 ['Do you speak anyway?', 'More often now. Being late to the sentence does not always mean being late to the decision.'],
 ['Does anyone help you get a word in?', 'Edrin asks whether anyone has not been heard. I appreciate that more than he probably realises.'],
 ['I sometimes let louder people choose.', 'So do I. I am trying to notice when I disagree before agreeing becomes a habit.']),
 t('What do you enjoy at the foundry?', 'The moment a complicated job becomes something everybody understands. All the preparation finally has a shape.',
 ['Is the work dangerous?', 'It deserves attention. I would rather explain that plainly than make it sound heroic.'],
 ['Do you work with friends?', 'Some became friends because we learned to rely on one another.'],
 ['What makes a good day?', 'A sound job and everyone leaving with the same number of fingers.']),
 t('Does Aurelius make you hopeful?', 'Yes, though I do not want to hand him responsibility for every hope I have.',
 ['He has enough to think about.', 'Then I shall be pleased to meet him without attaching a request.'],
 ['What are you hoping for?', 'More room for people to choose who they become. Seeing an unexpected friendship helps me imagine it.'],
 ['We cannot promise everything will be all right.', 'I would rather hear that honestly than be comforted by a promise you could not keep.']),
 t('Have you ever said something you were afraid to say?', 'I told a foreman we needed to stop and check a mould. I was shaking enough to be angry with myself.',
 ['Did he listen?', 'Yes. The check mattered. I try to remember the result instead of how my voice sounded.'],
 ['You still said it.', 'I did. I am learning to give myself credit for that part.'],
 ['Would you do it again?', 'Yes. I might still shake.']),
 t('What would you like to become braver about?', 'Expressing pleasure. I can deliver a warning more easily than tell someone their company matters to me.',
 ['You can practise with us.', 'Then I am glad you came back. There. A small beginning.'],
 ['Why is that harder?', 'A warning has a task attached. Affection leaves me feeling rather exposed.'],
 ['I think people would like hearing it.', 'So do I. That is why I am trying.']));

p('Sera Penn','Letter writer','Sera helps neighbours put difficult thoughts into letters and knows when the best sentence is a plain one.',
 ['I’m Sera Penn. A dragon has come through the door, and for once I cannot find a suitable sentence.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. “Welcome” has been a very good sentence so far.', 'Then welcome. I shall resist improving it.'],
 'Sera Penn. I help people with letters, though a conversation is a pleasant change of pace.',
 'A dragon travels with you? I hope someone at home receives news of how you both are, as well as the astonishing parts.',
 'Hello, Corin. What would you like to talk about?',
 t('What kind of letters do people ask for?', 'News, requests, apologies. They often begin by asking me to make a simple feeling sound impressive.',
 ['Do you?', 'I try to make it clear. Impressive can wait until the recipient understands what they mean.'],
 ['Are apologies difficult?', 'The ones that explain everything except what the writer is sorry for certainly are.'],
 ['Do you keep their stories private?', 'Of course. Helping someone speak is not permission to repeat what they said.']),
 t('Do you write letters for yourself?', 'Slowly. Advising someone else is much easier than deciding what I want to say to my own sister.',
 ['Do you get along?', 'Yes. That does not prevent me revising a perfectly affectionate paragraph seven times.'],
 ['What does she write back?', 'Usually a brisk note telling me to visit. She prefers conversation.'],
 ['You could send the first version.', 'I might. Please do not ask how many drafts I make of that decision.']),
 t('How would you describe Aurelius in a letter?', 'By beginning with what he did or said, rather than assuming “dragon” explains his character.',
 ['That would please him.', 'Then it would also be a more accurate letter.'],
 ['Would people believe you?', 'Some would ask questions. I would answer what I knew instead of making the account grander.'],
 ['Could you help me tell Nan about him?', 'If you wanted. I would begin by asking what you most wanted her to understand.']),
 t('Why does a letter matter so much?', 'Someone can return to it when the sender is far away. A small kindness may be read more than once.',
 ['Does that make you careful?', 'Yes. Especially with words a person might carry through a difficult week.'],
 ['What if I write something awkward?', 'An honest awkward sentence can mean more than perfect words that sound like somebody else.'],
 ['I miss hearing from home.', 'I hope your journey leaves opportunities for news to travel both ways.']),
 t('What would you tell us to write home?', 'Something ordinary as well as something important. The person reading wants to imagine you living, not only surviving danger.',
 ['What counts as ordinary?', 'A meal you liked. A person who made you laugh. A place you want to show them someday.'],
 ['I worry Nan will worry whatever I write.', 'She may. Knowing you thought of her can still make the waiting kinder.'],
 ['I could mention meeting you.', 'I would be pleased to become an ordinary good detail.']));

p('Halen Birch','Orchard worker','Halen trusts what he has observed, enjoys patient work, and has become wary of certainty delivered in a uniform.',
 ['Halen Birch. That is plainly a dragon, which settles one thing I have been told not to believe.', 'I’m Corin. This is Aurelius. I would rather you meet him than decide everything about him from a rumour.'],
 'Halen Birch. A visitor, then. What have you found along the road?',
 'You travel with a dragon? Then I would like to hear your own account before repeating someone else’s version.',
 'Corin. Good to see you again. How are you both getting on?',
 t('Do you like working in orchards?', 'Very much. Trees are demanding in a way I can understand, and they rarely pretend an urgent problem is somebody else’s fault.',
 ['What is your favourite season?', 'The first blossom. It makes all the cold work feel less theoretical.'],
 ['Is harvest the hardest part?', 'The busiest, usually. It is easier when people know how to work together.'],
 ['Do you ever get tired of fruit?', 'Only while sorting it. I recover with astonishing speed at supper.']),
 t('How do you decide which stories to believe?', 'I ask who actually saw the event and which parts they are guessing. Confidence is not the same as having been there.',
 ['Do people dislike being asked?', 'Some. Others are relieved to separate what they know from what they heard.'],
 ['Have you believed something foolish?', 'Certainly. That is why I ask now.'],
 ['What if nobody can be sure?', 'Then uncertainty is the honest answer for the moment.']),
 t('Does meeting a dragon change much for you?', 'It reminds me that the world can be larger than the account people in power prefer to give us.',
 ['Aurelius is more than evidence against Halvard.', 'You are right. I ought to ask how he is before turning him into an argument.'],
 ['What would you ask him?', 'What he has enjoyed discovering. That seems a fairer beginning.'],
 ['I am still surprised by our life sometimes.', 'Then I shall not be embarrassed by needing a moment myself.']),
 t('What have the orchards taught you?', 'That doing something at the wrong time can be worse than doing less. Enthusiasm cannot make a tree ready.',
 ['Is waiting difficult?', 'When the work matters, yes. Waiting carefully is still work.'],
 ['Does that apply to people?', 'Sometimes, but people can tell you what they need. It is polite to ask before comparing them to a tree.'],
 ['I am often impatient.', 'So am I. Having a lesson available does not mean I remember it every day.']),
 t('What are you looking forward to?', 'A season in which we can plan around the weather instead of another royal demand.',
 ['What would you do with a good harvest?', 'Make sure people were fed, pay the workers properly, and enjoy what remained.'],
 ['Would you celebrate?', 'Yes. Quietly at first, then less quietly if the neighbours arrived.'],
 ['That sounds worth hoping for.', 'I think so. Hope should have room for an ordinary good year.']));

p('Iria Dawn','Midwife’s assistant','Iria has learned to be calm without pretending to know everything, and saves her irreverence for people who need cheering.',
 ['I’m Iria Dawn. I had a hundred curious questions about dragons once. Seeing your companion makes “are you both well?” feel more useful.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. We are well enough to stop and talk. Thank you for asking.'],
 'Iria Dawn. Welcome. Have you had a difficult journey?',
 'A dragon companion. I hope somebody asks whether you have rested before asking for the whole story.',
 'Corin, hello. How are you, in the ordinary sense of the question?',
 t('What do you like about helping a midwife?', 'Being useful when a family is frightened and excited all at once. Sometimes the useful thing is surprisingly small.',
 ['Like what?', 'Getting the right person, keeping a room calm, remembering that someone has not eaten.'],
 ['Do you always know what to do?', 'No. I know when to ask the midwife instead of hiding uncertainty.'],
 ['That must be tiring.', 'Sometimes. It matters that we look after one another afterwards too.']),
 t('How do you help somebody feel calmer?', 'I tell them what I actually know and what will happen next. Invented reassurance tends to wear out at the worst moment.',
 ['What if there is nothing useful to say?', 'Then I can stay with them. Silence does not have to mean abandonment.'],
 ['Do jokes ever help?', 'With the right person. I try not to make someone laugh merely because I dislike seeing them upset.'],
 ['I prefer clear explanations too.', 'Most people do, especially when they are frightened.']),
 t('Would you know how to help an injured dragon?', 'No, and I would say so. Caring about someone does not supply knowledge I have never learned.',
 ['I appreciate the honest answer.', 'I could still help find what he needed. Admitting a limit is not the same as refusing to care.'],
 ['We keep food and supplies for him.', 'Then keep them in mind before an emergency. It is harder to plan when someone is hurt.'],
 ['I hope you never have to find out.', 'So do I. I would much rather meet him on an uneventful day.']),
 t('Who looks after you when you are tired?', 'Friends who notice when I begin organising everyone instead of admitting I need a rest.',
 ['Do you listen to them?', 'Eventually, with a theatrical amount of reluctance.'],
 ['Is it hard to stop being useful?', 'Yes. I am learning that my company is allowed to be enough.'],
 ['Aurelius notices when I am tired.', 'Then believe him occasionally. A friend may see what determination lets you ignore.']),
 t('What would you like for our next visit?', 'For you to tell me something you enjoyed. I am interested in your life, not merely whether you have survived it.',
 ['We have met some good people.', 'Then tell me about one of them.'],
 ['Some days just being safe feels enjoyable.', 'That counts. Pleasure need not impress anybody.'],
 ['This conversation has been a pleasant part.', 'I am glad. It has been one for me too.']));

p('Davin Rook','Apprentice cook','Davin enjoys feeding a crowd, tells stories against himself, and is trying to stop confusing confidence with competence.',
 ['I’m Davin Rook. I have just realised I know absolutely nothing about offering a dragon refreshments.', 'Corin, and Aurelius. A hello is enough. We have not arrived expecting you to feed us.'],
 'Davin Rook. Are you looking for someone, or staying to talk?',
 'A dragon travels with you? If anyone asks me what dragons eat, I shall now have the good sense to ask you first.',
 'Corin! Welcome back. I have several thoroughly ordinary subjects prepared.',
 t('Are you a good cook?', 'Improving. That is the answer my teacher allows me to give without interrupting.',
 ['What do you make well?', 'Roast vegetables. I finally stopped treating them as the part of supper nobody would inspect.'],
 ['What do you find difficult?', 'Having everything ready together. I can produce an excellent meal one inconvenient piece at a time.'],
 ['Do you enjoy learning?', 'Yes. Especially when the lesson can be eaten afterwards.']),
 t('What was your worst kitchen mistake?', 'I described a dish at length before discovering I had forgotten its main ingredient.',
 ['Could you rescue it?', 'We renamed it and served something else with it. I learned to inspect the meal before delivering its biography.'],
 ['Did anyone complain?', 'One person asked why I had sounded so certain. A devastatingly fair question.'],
 ['I have sounded certain while guessing too.', 'Then we belong to a very large and insufficiently quiet fellowship.']),
 t('Would you be nervous cooking for Aurelius?', 'A little. I would want to know his actual needs before making the meal into an occasion for myself.',
 ['Meat or fish helps keep him fed.', 'Useful and clear. Far better than the elaborate menu I might have invented.'],
 ['He is allowed to dislike something.', 'Of course. A guest should not have to flatter the cook into learning.'],
 ['We might just bring our own supplies.', 'Then I would be pleased to have your company without a culinary examination.']),
 t('Why do you come here?', 'People let me be useful while I am still learning. They also tell me when something needs changing, which is rarer than simple praise.',
 ['Do you cook for gatherings?', 'Sometimes. With help, and with less boasting every time.'],
 ['Does faith matter to you?', 'It does, though some days I understand it best as turning up for people.'],
 ['Can I visit without taking part?', 'Yes. Edrin is quite clear about that.']),
 t('What meal would you like to make someday?', 'One for everybody who tolerated my early cooking. It will contain every ingredient I claim it contains.',
 ['That is a promising start.', 'I am building the ambition on firm ground.'],
 ['Would you make something complicated?', 'Something good. I am trying to stop confusing the two.'],
 ['I hope they come.', 'I think they will. Kind people can also be curious about supper.']));

p('Mina Thorne','Grandparent and chapel regular','Mina enjoys children’s questions, remembers family customs without insisting everyone adopt them, and has an unexpectedly mischievous laugh.',
 ['I’m Mina Thorne. A dragon! My grandchildren are going to demand details I will certainly forget to notice.', 'Corin. His name is Aurelius. We can begin with our names; those are useful details.'],
 'Mina Thorne. Come and tell me what has brought you here.',
 'You travel with a dragon? I shall ask permission before making you the subject of an entire family evening.',
 'Hello, Corin. You are becoming a familiar face, which I enjoy.',
 t('What do your grandchildren ask about?', 'Whatever an adult has just tried to explain simply. Children have a talent for locating the missing part.',
 ['Do you enjoy their questions?', 'Very much, until the fifth question about why it is bedtime.'],
 ['Do they believe your stories?', 'They inspect them. I find that a healthy development, if occasionally inconvenient.'],
 ['Do you ever make things up?', 'For a tale, certainly. I tell them when we have entered a tale.']),
 t('Do you have family traditions?', 'We let the youngest person choose the first song at a gathering. We have endured some extraordinarily enthusiastic choices.',
 ['Why the youngest?', 'Because they spend so much time joining arrangements adults have already made.'],
 ['Can adults object?', 'After the first song. We are generous, not defenceless.'],
 ['Would you keep a tradition nobody liked?', 'No. The people matter more than continuing an inconvenience precisely.']),
 t('What would you tell a child meeting Aurelius?', 'Ask whether he wants to meet you. A marvellous creature is still allowed an opinion about the afternoon.',
 ['I wish every adult began there.', 'Then perhaps the children can improve the example.'],
 ['Would you tell them to be brave?', 'I would tell them they can look from farther away. Curiosity has no need to be hurried.'],
 ['He might enjoy their questions.', 'Then they would be delighted, and I would remind them to let him answer.']),
 t('What do you most enjoy about getting older?', 'I have stopped feeling obliged to enjoy things simply because everyone calls them excellent.',
 ['Does that include music?', 'Several very long pieces of it. I can admire the skill while wishing the musician would finish.'],
 ['Do you say so?', 'Tactfully, when possible. I still have to live among the people I tell.'],
 ['What do you enjoy without apology?', 'A ridiculous story told well, and people who laugh at their own importance.']),
 t('What would you like your grandchildren to inherit?', 'Stories they can question, affection they do not have to earn, and fewer things in boxes than I inherited.',
 ['That sounds generous.', 'It would also save them a great deal of sorting.'],
 ['Which story matters most?', 'That their family contained ordinary people who tried, failed, and tried again. They need not be perfect to belong to it.'],
 ['Nan has given me that sort of home.', 'Then I am glad, Corin. Tell her so when you can.']));

p('Perrin Clay','Brickmaker','Perrin takes pride in steady work and admits to dreams that are considerably less practical than his occupation.',
 ['Perrin Clay. I have practised a calm face for royal officials, but it appears not to work for dragons.', 'I’m Corin. This is Aurelius. You do not have to impress either of us with a calm face.'],
 'Perrin Clay. A pleasure to meet a new visitor. What brings you here?',
 'A dragon companion? Then I hope you meet people who can welcome you without first deciding what advantage it might bring them.',
 'Corin, hello. I have been looking forward to hearing how you are.',
 t('Do you enjoy making bricks?', 'I enjoy doing it well. I also enjoy the end of the working day, which seems a perfectly reasonable pair of feelings.',
 ['Can you tell your bricks from others?', 'Sometimes. Mostly I am pleased when nobody needs to think about the bricks at all.'],
 ['What makes a batch go wrong?', 'Several things. The trick is noticing before you have made the same mistake several hundred times.'],
 ['Do you ever want different work?', 'Occasionally. Wanting a change does not erase the years I have spent learning this.']),
 t('What would you do if you could choose anything?', 'Act in a play. I know, I look very much like a man who ought to have answered “more brickmaking”.',
 ['Why acting?', 'For an evening I could be someone with a completely different set of troubles.'],
 ['Have you tried it?', 'At a family gathering. My nephew directed and was merciless.'],
 ['What part would you want?', 'A king who gets shown the door. I suspect I could find the motivation.']),
 t('Would you put a dragon in a play?', 'Only if the story needed one. And I would not ask Aurelius to perform himself for our convenience.',
 ['He might enjoy being in the audience.', 'Then I would hope the play gave him more to enjoy than recognising the wings.'],
 ['People would argue about the costume.', 'People argue about every costume. Theatre is very generous with arguments.'],
 ['Could a dragon be the sensible character?', 'He might have to be. The humans in my favourite plays have very poor judgement.']),
 t('What makes you nervous about officials?', 'The possibility that an ordinary sentence will be taken as an insult by someone looking for one.',
 ['That is not really a conversation.', 'No. It is a guessing game with unequal consequences.'],
 ['Do you ever speak freely?', 'With friends, here, and more often when somebody else has begun.'],
 ['I dislike being spoken down to.', 'Most people do. They simply differ in how safely they can object.']),
 t('Have you thought more about acting?', 'Yes. I asked a few friends whether they would read a short scene with me. They said yes before I could explain why it was a foolish idea.',
 ['Perhaps it is not foolish.', 'I am beginning to suspect that.'],
 ['Will you play the king?', 'Someone else claimed the part. I am learning about artistic disappointment already.'],
 ['I would like to hear how it goes.', 'Then I have a reason to bring you news next time, instead of merely wishing.']));

p('Brother Orenfold','Chapel archivist','Orenfold keeps the congregation’s records and distrusts tidy accounts that leave the difficult parts out.',
 ['I am Brother Orenfold. A living dragon makes several confident old accounts look rather less complete.', 'Corin. This is Aurelius. We would be glad if you left some room in the account for what he says himself.'],
 'Brother Orenfold. Are you interested in this chapel’s history, or have you a different question?',
 'A dragon travels with you? Then the next record should begin with listening, not with finding a place for him in an old description.',
 'Welcome back, Corin. What would you like to ask?',
 t('What do you record?', 'Names, repairs, gifts, difficult decisions. The ordinary record often tells more truth than the grand anniversary account.',
 ['Why keep the difficult decisions?', 'Because a future reader deserves to know that people disagreed, and why.'],
 ['Do you write your own opinion?', 'When necessary, and I mark it as mine. Certainty should not be smuggled into a record by a tidy hand.'],
 ['What do people ask you to leave out?', 'Usually the part where they were mistaken. I understand the temptation.']),
 t('Have you ever changed an old record?', 'I add a correction when there is evidence. I prefer leaving a reader able to see what changed and why.',
 ['Even if the old version is embarrassing?', 'Especially then. Concealing the error makes the correction harder to trust.'],
 ['What if there are two accounts?', 'I keep both when I can. The disagreement is part of what we know.'],
 ['That sounds like patient work.', 'It is. A hurried certainty can take years to undo.']),
 t('How would you record meeting Aurelius?', 'With his name, the fact that he came with you, and only the details I actually observed or was told.',
 ['Would you ask his permission?', 'Yes, before recording something personal. A public visit does not make every thought public property.'],
 ['What if he corrects you?', 'Then I would thank him and correct the record.'],
 ['Would you write that you were amazed?', 'I might. It would be clearly my reaction, not a quality he was required to display.']),
 t('What should be remembered about the ban?', 'What was removed, who was ordered to remove it, and how people continued caring for one another afterwards.',
 ['Would you record who gave the orders?', 'Where we know it. Blame should be specific enough to be examined.'],
 ['Would you keep the hopeful parts too?', 'Certainly. A truthful account need not surrender every page to cruelty.'],
 ['Can people tell their own part?', 'I hope they will. I cannot write their memories for them.']),
 t('What would you ask us to preserve?', 'The names of the people who helped you, and the moments when you changed your minds. Both tend to disappear from heroic accounts.',
 ['Our story would be very long.', 'Then begin with a small true part. Completeness need not be the price of beginning.'],
 ['Will anyone want the uncertain parts?', 'Anyone trying to learn rather than merely admire.'],
 ['I would like Aurelius’s account beside mine.', 'That would make a more honest record than pretending you saw everything in the same way.']));

p('Brother Selwyn','Chapel host','Selwyn welcomes newcomers, enjoys simple jokes, and is careful not to confuse a kind invitation with a demand.',
 ['I am Brother Selwyn. Welcome, both of you. I shall ask about the dragon after making sure neither guest wants to leave immediately.', 'I’m Corin, and he is Aurelius. We would like to stay and talk.', 'Then that is an excellent beginning.'],
 'Brother Selwyn. Welcome. You may stay as long as you wish, and ask whatever you need to ask.',
 'You have a dragon companion? He would be welcome here if he wanted to visit. An invitation should leave room for an answer.',
 'Corin, welcome back. It is good to recognise someone without needing to keep them from leaving.',
 t('How do you welcome a stranger?', 'I try to tell them what they need to know before asking what they can tell me.',
 ['What do people need to know here?', 'That they may sit, ask questions, and leave without offending anyone.'],
 ['Do people arrive worried?', 'Some do. A new room has unwritten rules, and a newcomer cannot be expected to guess them all.'],
 ['Does anyone refuse the welcome?', 'Certainly. I try not to make refusing a second task they must complete.']),
 t('Have you ever felt out of place?', 'At a very fine dinner where I spent so long choosing the correct spoon that my soup became cold.',
 ['Did anybody help?', 'A woman beside me quietly used the same spoon I had chosen. I have never forgotten the kindness.'],
 ['Did you choose the wrong one?', 'I still do not know. That is rather the point.'],
 ['What would you do now?', 'Ask, or eat. I have become less willing to let a spoon defeat an evening.']),
 t('How should the chapel welcome Aurelius?', 'By asking what makes him comfortable and accepting an answer less ceremonial than we imagined.',
 ['He might like a quiet corner.', 'Then we can offer quiet. We need not fill it with explanations of how welcome he is.'],
 ['He might want to meet everyone.', 'Then introductions, at a pace he enjoys.'],
 ['What if he does not understand our customs?', 'We can explain without treating unfamiliarity as an offence.']),
 t('Do you ever get tired of meeting people?', 'Yes. Then I take a rest and let someone else welcome them. Tired kindness can become a rather tight smile.',
 ['You seem patient.', 'I have learned to rest before I begin resenting people for needing me.'],
 ['Does someone welcome you back?', 'Usually with a task and a joke. I consider it affection.'],
 ['That sounds like a sensible arrangement.', 'It is. A place ought to care for the people who keep it welcoming too.']),
 t('What would you like us to feel when we return?', 'That we are pleased to see you, and that you are free to come simply because you enjoy our company.',
 ['No great news required?', 'None. “We were passing” is a perfectly respectable reason.'],
 ['Aurelius deserves places like that.', 'So do you, Corin.'],
 ['Then we will remember this one.', 'I shall be glad to hear your hello again.']));

  return cast;
})();
